window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b096-4b418a835943ffc1.json"]={sha256:"4b418a835943ffc1ed9710c8448533e2549e94445cd0532a66660d37802a1bdc",value:{"id":"b096","title":"工程數位模型碰撞檢查","titleEn":"BIM-based construction clash detection","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從樓層高度預算與管線空間出發，說明聯合模型、共用座標與資訊容器如何讓各專業模型可比對，再處理硬碰撞與軟碰撞規則、模型發展程度、BCF 議題追蹤與區域簽認、4D 時空碰撞、誤報分組與模型品質、現場放樣公差，以及版本控制與資產資訊交接，並以 Crossrail 與巴黎路易威登基金會的公開資料對照。","summaryEn":"Starting from storey-height budgets and service space, explain how federated models, shared coordinates and information containers make discipline models comparable, then cover hard and clearance clash rules, level of development, BCF issue tracking and area sign-off, 4D space–time clashes, grouping of false positives and model quality, site set-out tolerances, version control and asset-information handover, compared with public material from Crossrail and the Fondation Louis Vuitton in Paris.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-facade-digital","subcategoryTitle":"帷幕牆、垂直運輸與數位營建","subcategoryTitleEn":"Facades, vertical transport and digital construction","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-facade-digital","learningTags":["structures","st-facade-digital","survey"],"architectureFamily":"survey","architectureNodes":[["各專業設計模型","Discipline design models"],["共用資料環境","Common data environment"],["聯合模型與碰撞規則","Federated model and clash rules"],["BCF 議題與協調會議","BCF issues and coordination meetings"],["現場放樣與竣工驗證","Site set-out and as-built verification"],["資產資訊模型","Asset information model"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,0],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"survey","labels":["各專業設計模型","共用資料環境","聯合模型與碰撞規則","BCF 議題與協調會議","現場放樣與竣工驗證"],"labelsEn":["Discipline design models","Common data environment","Federated model and clash rules","BCF issues and coordination meetings","Site set-out and as-built verification"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：一棟 20 層建築第一次聯合碰撞檢查得到 18,000 筆原始結果，分組後成為 900 組，其中 30% 即 270 組為真實議題。若這些議題留到現場，每件需 3 人工班 2 天（3×8×2 = 48 工時），以每工時 60 美元計為 2,880 美元，再加材料 1,200 美元，每件 4,080 美元，總計 270×4,080 = 1,101,600 美元。施工前協調由 2 名協調員做 26 週、每週 40 小時、每小時 75 美元，即 2×26×40×75 = 156,000 美元，加軟硬體 30,000 美元共 186,000 美元，效益比約 1,101,600/186,000 ≈ 5.9。若其中一半議題本來就會在製造圖階段被發現，效益減半為 550,800 美元，比值約 3.0，仍值得投入。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際專案。","textEn":"Design exercise: the first federated clash run on a 20-storey building returns 18,000 raw results, grouped into 900 groups, of which 30%, or 270, are real issues. Left to site, each would need a three-person crew for two days (3×8×2 = 48 labour-hours) at US$60 per hour, US$2,880, plus US$1,200 of material, US$4,080 each and 270×4,080 = US$1,101,600 in total. Pre-construction coordination by two coordinators for 26 weeks at 40 hours a week and US$75 per hour costs 2×26×40×75 = US$156,000, plus US$30,000 for software and hardware, US$186,000 in all, a benefit ratio of about 1,101,600/186,000 ≈ 5.9. If half the issues would have been caught at shop-drawing stage anyway, the benefit halves to US$550,800 and the ratio is about 3.0, still worth the effort. Values are teaching assumptions, not any real project.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b096-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「樓層高度預算與管線空間衝突」與「聯合模型、共用座標與資訊容器」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Storey-height budget and service-zone conflicts\" and \"Federated models, shared coordinates and information containers\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b096-v13-01","title":"樓層高度預算與管線空間衝突：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Storey-height budget and service-zone conflicts: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「天花板內管線空間」如何影響工程數位模型碰撞檢查的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ceiling service void” governs force, deformation or durability in “BIM-based construction clash detection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"碰撞多半不是軟體問題，而是空間預算問題：樓層高度一旦定案，結構梁深、天花板高度、架高地板與各類管線就要在固定的垂直空間中分配。風管斷面大且需要保溫，排水管必須依坡度下降，消防灑水支管與電纜架又各有間距要求，它們往往同時想佔用梁下方那一層最方便的空間。碰撞檢查真正的作用，是在施工前把這些搶空間的情況找出來，讓設計團隊重新分配管線層次、在梁腹開孔或調整風管斷面。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「天花板內管線空間」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Most clashes are not a software problem but a space-budget problem: once the storey height is fixed, beam depth, ceiling height, raised floor and every service must share a fixed vertical allowance. Ducts are large and need insulation, drainage pipes must fall at a gradient, and sprinkler branches and cable trays each have spacing rules, so they all compete for the same convenient layer just below the beams. The real purpose of clash detection is to expose these space conflicts before construction so the design team can re-layer the services, open beam webs or change duct sections. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Ceiling service void” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：樓高 4.20 m − 淨高 2.80 m − 天花板 0.05 m − 架高地板 0.15 m − 樓板 0.20 m = 樓板底至天花板 1.00 m；樓板下梁深 0.60 m，梁下只剩 0.40 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Storey 4.20 m − clear height 2.80 m − ceiling 0.05 m − raised floor 0.15 m − slab 0.20 m = 1.00 m from slab soffit to ceiling; with beams 0.60 m deep below the slab only 0.40 m remains under the beams.","failure":"常見誤解：「碰撞檢查的主要目的是找建模錯誤，與樓高設計無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Clash detection is mainly for catching modelling mistakes and has nothing to do with storey-height design.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「天花板內管線空間」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Ceiling service void”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-01-k1","title":"樓層高度預算與管線空間衝突","titleEn":"Storey-height budget and service-zone conflicts","text":"碰撞多半不是軟體問題，而是空間預算問題：樓層高度一旦定案，結構梁深、天花板高度、架高地板與各類管線就要在固定的垂直空間中分配。風管斷面大且需要保溫，排水管必須依坡度下降，消防灑水支管與電纜架又各有間距要求，它們往往同時想佔用梁下方那一層最方便的空間。","textEn":"Most clashes are not a software problem but a space-budget problem: once the storey height is fixed, beam depth, ceiling height, raised floor and every service must share a fixed vertical allowance. Ducts are large and need insulation, drainage pipes must fall at a gradient, and sprinkler branches and cable trays each have spacing rules, so they all compete for the same convenient layer just below the beams.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：碰撞檢查的主要目的是找建模錯誤，與樓高設計無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Clash detection is mainly for catching modelling mistakes and has nothing to do with storey-height design. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「樓層高度預算與管線空間衝突」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Storey-height budget and service-zone conflicts\" is correct?","options":["碰撞檢查的主要目的是找建模錯誤，與樓高設計無關。","碰撞多半不是軟體問題，而是空間預算問題：樓層高度一旦定案，結構梁深、天花板高度、架高地板與各類管線就要在固定的垂直空間中分配。","只要把所有檔案匯入同一個軟體，模型就會自動對齊。"],"optionsEn":["Clash detection is mainly for catching modelling mistakes and has nothing to do with storey-height design.","Most clashes are not a software problem but a space-budget problem: once the storey height is fixed, beam depth, ceiling height, raised floor and every service must share a fixed vertical allowance.","Importing every file into the same software aligns the models automatically."],"answer":1,"explanation":"碰撞多半不是軟體問題，而是空間預算問題：樓層高度一旦定案，結構梁深、天花板高度、架高地板與各類管線就要在固定的垂直空間中分配。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Most clashes are not a software problem but a space-budget problem: once the storey height is fixed, beam depth, ceiling height, raised floor and every service must share a fixed vertical allowance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b096-v13-02","title":"樓層高度預算與管線空間衝突：定量估算","titleEn":"Storey-height budget and service-zone conflicts: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「天花板內管線空間」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ceiling service void” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：樓高 4.20 m − 淨高 2.80 m − 天花板 0.05 m − 架高地板 0.15 m − 樓板 0.20 m = 樓板底至天花板 1.00 m；樓板下梁深 0.60 m，梁下只剩 0.40 m。0.45 m 高風管加保溫 2×0.025 m 與吊架 0.05 m 需 0.55 m，不足 0.15 m。若維持斷面積 0.45×1.00 = 0.45 m² 而把風管高度壓到 0.30 m，寬度需 0.45/0.30 = 1.5 m。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Storey 4.20 m − clear height 2.80 m − ceiling 0.05 m − raised floor 0.15 m − slab 0.20 m = 1.00 m from slab soffit to ceiling; with beams 0.60 m deep below the slab only 0.40 m remains under the beams. A 0.45 m duct plus 2×0.025 m insulation and a 0.05 m hanger needs 0.55 m, 0.15 m short. Keeping the area 0.45×1.00 = 0.45 m² but limiting the duct to 0.30 m high needs a width of 0.45/0.30 = 1.5 m. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在聯合模型中以剖面與平面標示每一樓層的管線分層區帶（例如梁下第一層給風管、第二層給水管），以碰撞檢查確認各專業物件都落在自己的區帶內；梁腹開孔要由結構工程師核算，並在模型中建立開孔物件，而不是讓管線直接穿梁。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: In the federated model, mark service layer zones on sections and plans for every floor (for example the first layer below the beams for ducts, the next for pipes) and use clash runs to confirm that each discipline's objects stay inside their zone; beam web openings must be checked by the structural engineer and modelled as opening objects rather than letting services pass through beams.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"樓高 4.20 m − 淨高 2.80 m − 天花板 0.05 m − 架高地板 0.15 m − 樓板 0.20 m = 樓板底至天花板 1.00 m；樓板下梁深 0.60 m，梁下只剩 0.40 m。0.45 m 高風管加保溫 2×0.025 m 與吊架 0.05 m 需 0.55 m，不足 0.15 m。若維持斷面積 0.45×1.00 = 0.45 m² 而把風管高度壓到 0.30 m，寬度需 0.45/0.30 = 1.5 m。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Storey 4.20 m − clear height 2.80 m − ceiling 0.05 m − raised floor 0.15 m − slab 0.20 m = 1.00 m from slab soffit to ceiling; with beams 0.60 m deep below the slab only 0.40 m remains under the beams. A 0.45 m duct plus 2×0.025 m insulation and a 0.05 m hanger needs 0.55 m, 0.15 m short. Keeping the area 0.45×1.00 = 0.45 m² but limiting the duct to 0.30 m high needs a width of 0.45/0.30 = 1.5 m. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「樓層高度預算與管線空間衝突」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Storey-height budget and service-zone conflicts\", which statement holds?","options":["所有元素都要做到最高的模型發展程度，碰撞檢查才有意義。","只要三維模型沒有碰撞，施工順序就不會發生衝突。","樓高 4.20 m − 淨高 2.80 m − 天花板 0.05 m − 架高地板 0.15 m − 樓板 0.20 m = 樓板底至天花板 1.00 m。"],"optionsEn":["Every element must reach the highest level of development for clash detection to be meaningful.","If the 3D model has no clashes, the construction sequence cannot conflict.","Storey 4.20 m − clear height 2.80 m − ceiling 0.05 m − raised floor 0.15 m − slab 0.20 m = 1.00 m from slab soffit to ceiling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"樓高 4.20 m − 淨高 2.80 m − 天花板 0.05 m − 架高地板 0.15 m − 樓板 0.20 m = 樓板底至天花板 1.00 m；樓板下梁深 0.60 m，梁下只剩 0.40 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Storey 4.20 m − clear height 2.80 m − ceiling 0.05 m − raised floor 0.15 m − slab 0.20 m = 1.00 m from slab soffit to ceiling; with beams 0.60 m deep below the slab only 0.40 m remains under the beams. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b096-v13-03","title":"樓層高度預算與管線空間衝突：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Storey-height budget and service-zone conflicts: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「天花板內管線空間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ceiling service void” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在聯合模型中以剖面與平面標示每一樓層的管線分層區帶（例如梁下第一層給風管、第二層給水管），以碰撞檢查確認各專業物件都落在自己的區帶內；梁腹開孔要由結構工程師核算，並在模型中建立開孔物件，而不是讓管線直接穿梁。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"In the federated model, mark service layer zones on sections and plans for every floor (for example the first layer below the beams for ducts, the next for pipes) and use clash runs to confirm that each discipline's objects stay inside their zone; beam web openings must be checked by the structural engineer and modelled as opening objects rather than letting services pass through beams. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在概念設計階段就由建築、結構與機電共同訂定典型樓層的垂直空間預算圖，列為設計凍結項目；之後任何梁深或淨高變更都必須重新簽認空間預算。","observationEn":"Site practice: At concept stage have architecture, structure and building services jointly agree a vertical space budget for typical floors and treat it as a design-freeze item; any later change to beam depth or clear height must re-sign the space budget.","failure":"注意干擾：樓高在初期為了增加樓層數被壓縮，管線空間卻沒有同步檢討，到施工圖階段才發現主風管無法通過梁下，只好降低天花板或在已澆置的梁上鑽孔；前者違反租約淨高，後者可能切斷鋼筋而需要結構補強。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Storey height squeezed early to gain floors, without a matching review of service space, reveals at shop-drawing stage that main ducts cannot pass under the beams, forcing either a lower ceiling that breaches lease clear heights or coring through cast beams that may cut reinforcement and require strengthening. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在聯合模型中以剖面與平面標示每一樓層的管線分層區帶（例如梁下第一層給風管、第二層給水管），以碰撞檢查確認各專業物件都落在自己的區帶內；梁腹開孔要由結構工程師核算，並在模型中建立開孔物件，而不是讓管線直接穿梁。","textEn":"In the federated model, mark service layer zones on sections and plans for every floor (for example the first layer below the beams for ducts, the next for pipes) and use clash runs to confirm that each discipline's objects stay inside their zone; beam web openings must be checked by the structural engineer and modelled as opening objects rather than letting services pass through beams.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在概念設計階段就由建築、結構與機電共同訂定典型樓層的垂直空間預算圖，列為設計凍結項目；之後任何梁深或淨高變更都必須重新簽認空間預算。","textEn":"At concept stage have architecture, structure and building services jointly agree a vertical space budget for typical floors and treat it as a design-freeze item; any later change to beam depth or clear height must re-sign the space budget.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「樓層高度預算與管線空間衝突」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Storey-height budget and service-zone conflicts\"?","options":["在聯合模型中以剖面與平面標示每一樓層的管線分層區帶（例如梁下第一層給風管、第二層給水管），以碰撞檢查確認各專業物件都落在自己的區帶內。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","模型協調完成後，現場只要照圖施工就不會有空間衝突。"],"optionsEn":["In the federated model, mark service layer zones on sections and plans for every floor (for example the first layer below the beams for ducts, the next for pipes) and use clash runs to confirm that each discipline's objects stay inside their zone.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Once the model is coordinated, building to the drawings cannot produce space conflicts."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在聯合模型中以剖面與平面標示每一樓層的管線分層區帶（例如梁下第一層給風管、第二層給水管），以碰撞檢查確認各專業物件都落在自己的區帶內；梁腹開孔要由結構工程師核算，並在模型中建立開孔物件，而不是讓管線直接穿梁。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"In the federated model, mark service layer zones on sections and plans for every floor (for example the first layer below the beams for ducts, the next for pipes) and use clash runs to confirm that each discipline's objects stay inside their zone; beam web openings must be checked by the structural engineer and modelled as opening objects rather than letting services pass through beams. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b096-v13-04","title":"樓層高度預算與管線空間衝突：失效診斷","titleEn":"Storey-height budget and service-zone conflicts: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「天花板內管線空間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ceiling service void” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"樓高在初期為了增加樓層數被壓縮，管線空間卻沒有同步檢討，到施工圖階段才發現主風管無法通過梁下，只好降低天花板或在已澆置的梁上鑽孔；前者違反租約淨高，後者可能切斷鋼筋而需要結構補強。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Storey height squeezed early to gain floors, without a matching review of service space, reveals at shop-drawing stage that main ducts cannot pass under the beams, forcing either a lower ceiling that breaches lease clear heights or coring through cast beams that may cut reinforcement and require strengthening. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：碰撞檢查真正的作用，是在施工前把這些搶空間的情況找出來，讓設計團隊重新分配管線層次、在梁腹開孔或調整風管斷面。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The real purpose of clash detection is to expose these space conflicts before construction so the design team can re-layer the services, open beam webs or change duct sections.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「碰撞檢查的主要目的是找建模錯誤，與樓高設計無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Clash detection is mainly for catching modelling mistakes and has nothing to do with storey-height design.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"樓高在初期為了增加樓層數被壓縮，管線空間卻沒有同步檢討，到施工圖階段才發現主風管無法通過梁下，只好降低天花板或在已澆置的梁上鑽孔；前者違反租約淨高，後者可能切斷鋼筋而需要結構補強。","textEn":"Storey height squeezed early to gain floors, without a matching review of service space, reveals at shop-drawing stage that main ducts cannot pass under the beams, forcing either a lower ceiling that breaches lease clear heights or coring through cast beams that may cut reinforcement and require strengthening.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「樓層高度預算與管線空間衝突」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Storey-height budget and service-zone conflicts\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","樓高在初期為了增加樓層數被壓縮，管線空間卻沒有同步檢討，到施工圖階段才發現主風管無法通過梁下，只好降低天花板或在已澆置的梁上鑽孔。","只要把所有檔案匯入同一個軟體，模型就會自動對齊。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Storey height squeezed early to gain floors, without a matching review of service space, reveals at shop-drawing stage that main ducts cannot pass under the beams, forcing either a lower ceiling that breaches lease clear heights or coring through cast beams that may cut reinforcement and require strengthening.","Importing every file into the same software aligns the models automatically."],"answer":1,"explanation":"樓高在初期為了增加樓層數被壓縮，管線空間卻沒有同步檢討，到施工圖階段才發現主風管無法通過梁下，只好降低天花板或在已澆置的梁上鑽孔；前者違反租約淨高，後者可能切斷鋼筋而需要結構補強。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Storey height squeezed early to gain floors, without a matching review of service space, reveals at shop-drawing stage that main ducts cannot pass under the beams, forcing either a lower ceiling that breaches lease clear heights or coring through cast beams that may cut reinforcement and require strengthening. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b096-v13-05","title":"聯合模型、共用座標與資訊容器：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Federated models, shared coordinates and information containers: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「共用座標原點」如何影響工程數位模型碰撞檢查的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Shared coordinate origin” governs force, deformation or durability in “BIM-based construction clash detection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"各專業通常在不同軟體、不同檔案中建模，碰撞檢查前要把它們組成聯合模型；聯合時各模型互不改動，只是疊在一起比對，Crossrail 的 BIM 經驗也強調個別模型不互相影響，必須由模型管理者確認它們彼此吻合。要能正確疊合，所有模型必須使用同一個專案原點、同一個方位角與同一個高程基準，並依 ISO 19650 的資訊容器規則命名與分割，讓每個檔案的責任人、狀態與版本都清楚。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「共用座標原點」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Each discipline usually models in its own software and files, so before clash runs they are assembled into a federated model; the models are overlaid and compared without altering one another, and Crossrail's BIM lessons likewise stress that individual models do not interact and that the model steward must confirm they fit together. To overlay correctly, every model must use the same project origin, the same rotation to grid north and the same height datum, and be named and split as information containers under ISO 19650 so that each file's owner, status and revision are clear. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Shared coordinate origin” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：旋轉誤差造成的位移 d = L·sin θ。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Offset from a rotation error d = L·sin θ.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要把所有檔案匯入同一個軟體，模型就會自動對齊。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Importing every file into the same software aligns the models automatically.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「共用座標原點」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Shared coordinate origin”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-05-k1","title":"聯合模型、共用座標與資訊容器","titleEn":"Federated models, shared coordinates and information containers","text":"各專業通常在不同軟體、不同檔案中建模，碰撞檢查前要把它們組成聯合模型；聯合時各模型互不改動，只是疊在一起比對，Crossrail 的 BIM 經驗也強調個別模型不互相影響，必須由模型管理者確認它們彼此吻合。要能正確疊合，所有模型必須使用同一個專案原點、同一個方位角與同一個高程基準，並依 ISO 19650 的資訊容器規則命名與分割，讓每個檔案的責任人、狀態與版本都清楚。","textEn":"Each discipline usually models in its own software and files, so before clash runs they are assembled into a federated model; the models are overlaid and compared without altering one another, and Crossrail's BIM lessons likewise stress that individual models do not interact and that the model steward must confirm they fit together. To overlay correctly, every model must use the same project origin, the same rotation to grid north and the same height datum, and be named and split as information containers under ISO 19650 so that each file's owner, status and revision are clear.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要把所有檔案匯入同一個軟體，模型就會自動對齊。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Importing every file into the same software aligns the models automatically. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「聯合模型、共用座標與資訊容器」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Federated models, shared coordinates and information containers\" is correct?","options":["只要把所有檔案匯入同一個軟體，模型就會自動對齊。","碰撞報告為零，就代表現場一定可以順利安裝。","各專業通常在不同軟體、不同檔案中建模，碰撞檢查前要把它們組成聯合模型。"],"optionsEn":["Importing every file into the same software aligns the models automatically.","A clash report of zero guarantees smooth installation on site.","Each discipline usually models in its own software and files, so before clash runs they are assembled into a federated model."],"answer":2,"explanation":"各專業通常在不同軟體、不同檔案中建模，碰撞檢查前要把它們組成聯合模型；聯合時各模型互不改動，只是疊在一起比對，Crossrail 的 BIM 經驗也強調個別模型不互相影響，必須由模型管理者確認它們彼此吻合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Each discipline usually models in its own software and files, so before clash runs they are assembled into a federated model; the models are overlaid and compared without altering one another, and Crossrail's BIM lessons likewise stress that individual models do not interact and that the model steward must confirm they fit together. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b096-v13-06","title":"聯合模型、共用座標與資訊容器：定量估算","titleEn":"Federated models, shared coordinates and information containers: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「共用座標原點」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Shared coordinate origin” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：旋轉誤差造成的位移 d = L·sin θ。建築長 120 m、兩模型方位差 0.5°：d = 120×sin 0.5° = 120×0.00873 ≈ 1.05 m；即使只差 0.05°，遠端仍偏約 0.10 m，足以產生大量假碰撞。單位若誤設為公尺與公釐之差，尺度相差 1,000 倍。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Offset from a rotation error d = L·sin θ. For a 120 m building with a 0.5° rotation mismatch, d = 120×sin 0.5° = 120×0.00873 ≈ 1.05 m; even 0.05° leaves about 0.10 m at the far end, enough to create many false clashes. A unit mix-up between metres and millimetres scales the model by 1,000. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在每個模型中放置相同的座標檢核物件（例如三個角落的格線交點與測量控制點），聯合後量測它們的偏差，要求小於約 1 mm；並檢查單位、樓層高程表與檔名規則，未通過者退回原作者，不得進入碰撞檢查。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Place identical coordinate check objects in every model (for example grid intersections at three corners and survey control points), measure their deviation after federation and require it to be below about 1 mm; also check units, level tables and naming rules, and return any failing model to its author before it enters clash runs.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"旋轉誤差造成的位移 d = L·sin θ。建築長 120 m、兩模型方位差 0.5°：d = 120×sin 0.5° = 120×0.00873 ≈ 1.05 m；即使只差 0.05°，遠端仍偏約 0.10 m，足以產生大量假碰撞。單位若誤設為公尺與公釐之差，尺度相差 1,000 倍。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Offset from a rotation error d = L·sin θ. For a 120 m building with a 0.5° rotation mismatch, d = 120×sin 0.5° = 120×0.00873 ≈ 1.05 m; even 0.05° leaves about 0.10 m at the far end, enough to create many false clashes. A unit mix-up between metres and millimetres scales the model by 1,000. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「聯合模型、共用座標與資訊容器」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Federated models, shared coordinates and information containers\", which statement holds?","options":["旋轉誤差造成的位移 d = L·sin θ。","碰撞報告產出後，軟體會自動決定哪個專業必須修改。","碰撞數量越少，代表協調品質越好。"],"optionsEn":["Offset from a rotation error d = L·sin θ.","Once the clash report is produced, the software decides which discipline must change.","The fewer the clashes in the report, the better the coordination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"旋轉誤差造成的位移 d = L·sin θ。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Offset from a rotation error d = L·sin θ. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b096-v13-07","title":"聯合模型、共用座標與資訊容器：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Federated models, shared coordinates and information containers: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「共用座標原點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Shared coordinate origin” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在每個模型中放置相同的座標檢核物件（例如三個角落的格線交點與測量控制點），聯合後量測它們的偏差，要求小於約 1 mm；並檢查單位、樓層高程表與檔名規則，未通過者退回原作者，不得進入碰撞檢查。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Place identical coordinate check objects in every model (for example grid intersections at three corners and survey control points), measure their deviation after federation and require it to be below about 1 mm; also check units, level tables and naming rules, and return any failing model to its author before it enters clash runs. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：BIM 執行計畫應明列專案座標系統、原點、方位角、高程基準、單位與檔案分割原則，由資訊管理者在每次聯合前執行座標檢核；未通過檢核的模型不得改為「共享」狀態。","observationEn":"Site practice: The BIM execution plan should state the project coordinate system, origin, rotation, height datum, units and file-splitting rules, and the information manager should run the coordinate check before every federation; a model that fails cannot be moved to Shared status.","failure":"注意干擾：機電模型以本地原點建立而未對齊結構模型時，第一次碰撞報告可能出現數萬筆假碰撞，團隊為了消化報告而放寬容許值或關閉部分測試，真正的碰撞反而被淹沒。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An MEP model built on a local origin and not aligned to the structural model can produce tens of thousands of false clashes in the first report, and teams trying to digest it widen tolerances or switch off tests, burying the real clashes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在每個模型中放置相同的座標檢核物件（例如三個角落的格線交點與測量控制點），聯合後量測它們的偏差，要求小於約 1 mm；並檢查單位、樓層高程表與檔名規則，未通過者退回原作者，不得進入碰撞檢查。","textEn":"Place identical coordinate check objects in every model (for example grid intersections at three corners and survey control points), measure their deviation after federation and require it to be below about 1 mm; also check units, level tables and naming rules, and return any failing model to its author before it enters clash runs.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"BIM 執行計畫應明列專案座標系統、原點、方位角、高程基準、單位與檔案分割原則，由資訊管理者在每次聯合前執行座標檢核；未通過檢核的模型不得改為「共享」狀態。","textEn":"The BIM execution plan should state the project coordinate system, origin, rotation, height datum, units and file-splitting rules, and the information manager should run the coordinate check before every federation; a model that fails cannot be moved to Shared status.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「聯合模型、共用座標與資訊容器」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Federated models, shared coordinates and information containers\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在每個模型中放置相同的座標檢核物件（例如三個角落的格線交點與測量控制點），聯合後量測它們的偏差，要求小於約 1 mm。","共用資料環境只是存放檔案的雲端資料夾。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Place identical coordinate check objects in every model (for example grid intersections at three corners and survey control points), measure their deviation after federation and require it to be below about 1 mm.","A common data environment is just a cloud folder for storing files."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在每個模型中放置相同的座標檢核物件（例如三個角落的格線交點與測量控制點），聯合後量測它們的偏差，要求小於約 1 mm；並檢查單位、樓層高程表與檔名規則，未通過者退回原作者，不得進入碰撞檢查。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Place identical coordinate check objects in every model (for example grid intersections at three corners and survey control points), measure their deviation after federation and require it to be below about 1 mm; also check units, level tables and naming rules, and return any failing model to its author before it enters clash runs. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b096-v13-08","title":"聯合模型、共用座標與資訊容器：失效診斷","titleEn":"Federated models, shared coordinates and information containers: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「共用座標原點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Shared coordinate origin” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"機電模型以本地原點建立而未對齊結構模型時，第一次碰撞報告可能出現數萬筆假碰撞，團隊為了消化報告而放寬容許值或關閉部分測試，真正的碰撞反而被淹沒。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An MEP model built on a local origin and not aligned to the structural model can produce tens of thousands of false clashes in the first report, and teams trying to digest it widen tolerances or switch off tests, burying the real clashes. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：要能正確疊合，所有模型必須使用同一個專案原點、同一個方位角與同一個高程基準，並依 ISO 19650 的資訊容器規則命名與分割，讓每個檔案的責任人、狀態與版本都清楚。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: To overlay correctly, every model must use the same project origin, the same rotation to grid north and the same height datum, and be named and split as information containers under ISO 19650 so that each file's owner, status and revision are clear.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要把所有檔案匯入同一個軟體，模型就會自動對齊。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Importing every file into the same software aligns the models automatically.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"機電模型以本地原點建立而未對齊結構模型時，第一次碰撞報告可能出現數萬筆假碰撞，團隊為了消化報告而放寬容許值或關閉部分測試，真正的碰撞反而被淹沒。","textEn":"An MEP model built on a local origin and not aligned to the structural model can produce tens of thousands of false clashes in the first report, and teams trying to digest it widen tolerances or switch off tests, burying the real clashes.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「聯合模型、共用座標與資訊容器」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Federated models, shared coordinates and information containers\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","碰撞報告為零，就代表現場一定可以順利安裝。","機電模型以本地原點建立而未對齊結構模型時，第一次碰撞報告可能出現數萬筆假碰撞，團隊為了消化報告而放寬容許值或關閉部分測試，真正的碰撞反而被淹沒。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A clash report of zero guarantees smooth installation on site.","An MEP model built on a local origin and not aligned to the structural model can produce tens of thousands of false clashes in the first report, and teams trying to digest it widen tolerances or switch off tests, burying the real clashes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"機電模型以本地原點建立而未對齊結構模型時，第一次碰撞報告可能出現數萬筆假碰撞，團隊為了消化報告而放寬容許值或關閉部分測試，真正的碰撞反而被淹沒。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An MEP model built on a local origin and not aligned to the structural model can produce tens of thousands of false clashes in the first report, and teams trying to digest it widen tolerances or switch off tests, burying the real clashes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b096-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「硬碰撞、軟碰撞與容許值設定」與「模型發展程度與細部碰撞」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Hard clashes, clearance clashes and tolerance settings\" and \"Level of development and detail clashes\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b096-v13-09","title":"硬碰撞、軟碰撞與容許值設定：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Hard clashes, clearance clashes and tolerance settings: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「碰撞規則與容許值」如何影響工程數位模型碰撞檢查的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Clash rules and tolerances” governs force, deformation or durability in “BIM-based construction clash detection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"硬碰撞是兩個實體幾何直接重疊，例如風管穿過梁；軟碰撞（淨距碰撞）則是物件之間的距離小於規定淨距，例如保溫層、維修空間、灑水頭下方淨空或電纜與熱水管的間隔。碰撞軟體只比對幾何與規則，所以容許值設定決定報告的意義：容許值太小會把接觸與建模誤差都報出來，太大則漏掉真正問題；保溫層、防火被覆是否建模，也會讓同一配置出現或不出現碰撞。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「碰撞規則與容許值」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A hard clash is a direct overlap of two solids, such as a duct passing through a beam; a soft or clearance clash is a distance below a required clearance, such as insulation, maintenance access, sprinkler deflector clearance or separation between cables and hot-water pipes. Clash software only compares geometry against rules, so tolerance settings decide what a report means: too small a tolerance reports touching objects and modelling noise, too large misses real problems, and whether insulation or fireproofing is modelled decides whether the same layout clashes at all. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Clash rules and tolerances” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：兩支外徑 150 mm 的管線中心距 160 mm：裸管間隙 160 − 150 = 10 mm，無硬碰撞。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Two 150 mm OD pipes at 160 mm centres: bare gap 160 − 150 = 10 mm, no hard clash.","failure":"常見誤解：「碰撞報告為零，就代表現場一定可以順利安裝。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A clash report of zero guarantees smooth installation on site.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「碰撞規則與容許值」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Clash rules and tolerances”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-09-k1","title":"硬碰撞、軟碰撞與容許值設定","titleEn":"Hard clashes, clearance clashes and tolerance settings","text":"硬碰撞是兩個實體幾何直接重疊，例如風管穿過梁；軟碰撞（淨距碰撞）則是物件之間的距離小於規定淨距，例如保溫層、維修空間、灑水頭下方淨空或電纜與熱水管的間隔。碰撞軟體只比對幾何與規則，所以容許值設定決定報告的意義：容許值太小會把接觸與建模誤差都報出來，太大則漏掉真正問題；保溫層、防火被覆是否建模，也會讓同一配置出現或不出現碰撞。","textEn":"A hard clash is a direct overlap of two solids, such as a duct passing through a beam; a soft or clearance clash is a distance below a required clearance, such as insulation, maintenance access, sprinkler deflector clearance or separation between cables and hot-water pipes. Clash software only compares geometry against rules, so tolerance settings decide what a report means: too small a tolerance reports touching objects and modelling noise, too large misses real problems, and whether insulation or fireproofing is modelled decides whether the same layout clashes at all.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：碰撞報告為零，就代表現場一定可以順利安裝。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A clash report of zero guarantees smooth installation on site. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「硬碰撞、軟碰撞與容許值設定」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Hard clashes, clearance clashes and tolerance settings\" is correct?","options":["硬碰撞是兩個實體幾何直接重疊，例如風管穿過梁；軟碰撞（淨距碰撞）則是物件之間的距離小於規定淨距，例如保溫層、維修空間、灑水頭下方淨空或電纜與熱水管的間隔。","碰撞報告為零，就代表現場一定可以順利安裝。","所有元素都要做到最高的模型發展程度，碰撞檢查才有意義。"],"optionsEn":["A hard clash is a direct overlap of two solids, such as a duct passing through a beam.","A clash report of zero guarantees smooth installation on site.","Every element must reach the highest level of development for clash detection to be meaningful."],"answer":0,"explanation":"硬碰撞是兩個實體幾何直接重疊，例如風管穿過梁；軟碰撞（淨距碰撞）則是物件之間的距離小於規定淨距，例如保溫層、維修空間、灑水頭下方淨空或電纜與熱水管的間隔。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A hard clash is a direct overlap of two solids, such as a duct passing through a beam; a soft or clearance clash is a distance below a required clearance, such as insulation, maintenance access, sprinkler deflector clearance or separation between cables and hot-water pipes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b096-v13-10","title":"硬碰撞、軟碰撞與容許值設定：定量估算","titleEn":"Hard clashes, clearance clashes and tolerance settings: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「碰撞規則與容許值」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Clash rules and tolerances” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：兩支外徑 150 mm 的管線中心距 160 mm：裸管間隙 160 − 150 = 10 mm，無硬碰撞。各加 25 mm 保溫後外徑 200 mm，重疊 200 − 160 = 40 mm。若規定保溫面之間淨距 50 mm，所需中心距 200 + 50 = 250 mm，須再移開 90 mm。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Two 150 mm OD pipes at 160 mm centres: bare gap 160 − 150 = 10 mm, no hard clash. With 25 mm insulation each the outer diameter is 200 mm and the overlap is 200 − 160 = 40 mm. A 50 mm clearance rule between insulation faces needs 200 + 50 = 250 mm centres, another 90 mm apart. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：為每一組專業配對建立碰撞矩陣，寫明硬碰撞容許值、軟碰撞淨距與排除條件（例如同系統的接頭、穿越套管），先以刻意放入的已知碰撞樣本測試規則是否抓得到；規則每次修改都要記錄版本，以免前後報告數量無法比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build a clash matrix for every discipline pair stating hard-clash tolerance, clearance distances and exclusions (for example joints within one system or penetrations through sleeves), test the rules first on seeded known clashes to confirm they are caught, and version every rule change so that report counts remain comparable over time.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"兩支外徑 150 mm 的管線中心距 160 mm：裸管間隙 160 − 150 = 10 mm，無硬碰撞。各加 25 mm 保溫後外徑 200 mm，重疊 200 − 160 = 40 mm。若規定保溫面之間淨距 50 mm，所需中心距 200 + 50 = 250 mm，須再移開 90 mm。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Two 150 mm OD pipes at 160 mm centres: bare gap 160 − 150 = 10 mm, no hard clash. With 25 mm insulation each the outer diameter is 200 mm and the overlap is 200 − 160 = 40 mm. A 50 mm clearance rule between insulation faces needs 200 + 50 = 250 mm centres, another 90 mm apart. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「硬碰撞、軟碰撞與容許值設定」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Hard clashes, clearance clashes and tolerance settings\", which statement holds?","options":["只要三維模型沒有碰撞，施工順序就不會發生衝突。","兩支外徑 150 mm 的管線中心距 160 mm：裸管間隙 160 − 150 = 10 mm，無硬碰撞。","模型協調完成後，現場只要照圖施工就不會有空間衝突。"],"optionsEn":["If the 3D model has no clashes, the construction sequence cannot conflict.","Two 150 mm OD pipes at 160 mm centres: bare gap 160 − 150 = 10 mm, no hard clash.","Once the model is coordinated, building to the drawings cannot produce space conflicts."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩支外徑 150 mm 的管線中心距 160 mm：裸管間隙 160 − 150 = 10 mm，無硬碰撞。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Two 150 mm OD pipes at 160 mm centres: bare gap 160 − 150 = 10 mm, no hard clash. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b096-v13-11","title":"硬碰撞、軟碰撞與容許值設定：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Hard clashes, clearance clashes and tolerance settings: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「碰撞規則與容許值」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Clash rules and tolerances” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"為每一組專業配對建立碰撞矩陣，寫明硬碰撞容許值、軟碰撞淨距與排除條件（例如同系統的接頭、穿越套管），先以刻意放入的已知碰撞樣本測試規則是否抓得到；規則每次修改都要記錄版本，以免前後報告數量無法比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build a clash matrix for every discipline pair stating hard-clash tolerance, clearance distances and exclusions (for example joints within one system or penetrations through sleeves), test the rules first on seeded known clashes to confirm they are caught, and version every rule change so that report counts remain comparable over time. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：碰撞矩陣與容許值應在 BIM 執行計畫中定案並由各專業設計負責人簽認；保溫、防火被覆、維修與操作淨空必須以實體或淨空體積建模，不能只寫在說明中。","observationEn":"Site practice: Finalise the clash matrix and tolerances in the BIM execution plan with sign-off from each discipline lead; insulation, fireproofing and maintenance or operating clearances must be modelled as solids or clearance volumes, not left in notes.","failure":"注意干擾：規則若未包含保溫層或維修淨空，報告顯示零碰撞，現場卻發現保溫後的管線互相擠壓、閥門無法操作，只能拆除重排；反之把同系統接頭也列為碰撞，報告數量膨脹到無法審查。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Rules that omit insulation or maintenance clearance show zero clashes, yet on site insulated pipes are squeezed together and valves cannot be operated, forcing removal and re-routing; conversely, counting joints within one system as clashes inflates reports beyond any chance of review. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"為每一組專業配對建立碰撞矩陣，寫明硬碰撞容許值、軟碰撞淨距與排除條件（例如同系統的接頭、穿越套管），先以刻意放入的已知碰撞樣本測試規則是否抓得到；規則每次修改都要記錄版本，以免前後報告數量無法比較。","textEn":"Build a clash matrix for every discipline pair stating hard-clash tolerance, clearance distances and exclusions (for example joints within one system or penetrations through sleeves), test the rules first on seeded known clashes to confirm they are caught, and version every rule change so that report counts remain comparable over time.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"碰撞矩陣與容許值應在 BIM 執行計畫中定案並由各專業設計負責人簽認；保溫、防火被覆、維修與操作淨空必須以實體或淨空體積建模，不能只寫在說明中。","textEn":"Finalise the clash matrix and tolerances in the BIM execution plan with sign-off from each discipline lead; insulation, fireproofing and maintenance or operating clearances must be modelled as solids or clearance volumes, not left in notes.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「硬碰撞、軟碰撞與容許值設定」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Hard clashes, clearance clashes and tolerance settings\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","施工期間協調用的模型就等於竣工模型。","為每一組專業配對建立碰撞矩陣，寫明硬碰撞容許值、軟碰撞淨距與排除條件（例如同系統的接頭、穿越套管），先以刻意放入的已知碰撞樣本測試規則是否抓得到。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The model used for coordination during construction is the as-built model.","Build a clash matrix for every discipline pair stating hard-clash tolerance, clearance distances and exclusions (for example joints within one system or penetrations through sleeves), test the rules first on seeded known clashes to confirm they are caught, and version every rule change so that report counts remain comparable over time."],"answer":2,"explanation":"為每一組專業配對建立碰撞矩陣，寫明硬碰撞容許值、軟碰撞淨距與排除條件（例如同系統的接頭、穿越套管），先以刻意放入的已知碰撞樣本測試規則是否抓得到；規則每次修改都要記錄版本，以免前後報告數量無法比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build a clash matrix for every discipline pair stating hard-clash tolerance, clearance distances and exclusions (for example joints within one system or penetrations through sleeves), test the rules first on seeded known clashes to confirm they are caught, and version every rule change so that report counts remain comparable over time. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b096-v13-12","title":"硬碰撞、軟碰撞與容許值設定：失效診斷","titleEn":"Hard clashes, clearance clashes and tolerance settings: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「碰撞規則與容許值」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Clash rules and tolerances” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"規則若未包含保溫層或維修淨空，報告顯示零碰撞，現場卻發現保溫後的管線互相擠壓、閥門無法操作，只能拆除重排；反之把同系統接頭也列為碰撞，報告數量膨脹到無法審查。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Rules that omit insulation or maintenance clearance show zero clashes, yet on site insulated pipes are squeezed together and valves cannot be operated, forcing removal and re-routing; conversely, counting joints within one system as clashes inflates reports beyond any chance of review. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：碰撞軟體只比對幾何與規則，所以容許值設定決定報告的意義：容許值太小會把接觸與建模誤差都報出來，太大則漏掉真正問題；保溫層、防火被覆是否建模，也會讓同一配置出現或不出現碰撞。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Clash software only compares geometry against rules, so tolerance settings decide what a report means: too small a tolerance reports touching objects and modelling noise, too large misses real problems, and whether insulation or fireproofing is modelled decides whether the same layout clashes at all.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「碰撞報告為零，就代表現場一定可以順利安裝。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A clash report of zero guarantees smooth installation on site.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"規則若未包含保溫層或維修淨空，報告顯示零碰撞，現場卻發現保溫後的管線互相擠壓、閥門無法操作，只能拆除重排；反之把同系統接頭也列為碰撞，報告數量膨脹到無法審查。","textEn":"Rules that omit insulation or maintenance clearance show zero clashes, yet on site insulated pipes are squeezed together and valves cannot be operated, forcing removal and re-routing; conversely, counting joints within one system as clashes inflates reports beyond any chance of review.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「硬碰撞、軟碰撞與容許值設定」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Hard clashes, clearance clashes and tolerance settings\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["規則若未包含保溫層或維修淨空，報告顯示零碰撞，現場卻發現保溫後的管線互相擠壓、閥門無法操作，只能拆除重排；反之把同系統接頭也列為碰撞，報告數量膨脹到無法審查。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","所有元素都要做到最高的模型發展程度，碰撞檢查才有意義。"],"optionsEn":["Rules that omit insulation or maintenance clearance show zero clashes, yet on site insulated pipes are squeezed together and valves cannot be operated, forcing removal and re-routing.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Every element must reach the highest level of development for clash detection to be meaningful."],"answer":0,"explanation":"規則若未包含保溫層或維修淨空，報告顯示零碰撞，現場卻發現保溫後的管線互相擠壓、閥門無法操作，只能拆除重排；反之把同系統接頭也列為碰撞，報告數量膨脹到無法審查。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Rules that omit insulation or maintenance clearance show zero clashes, yet on site insulated pipes are squeezed together and valves cannot be operated, forcing removal and re-routing; conversely, counting joints within one system as clashes inflates reports beyond any chance of review. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b096-v13-13","title":"模型發展程度與細部碰撞：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Level of development and detail clashes: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「鋼筋與預埋件密度」如何影響工程數位模型碰撞檢查的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rebar and embed congestion” governs force, deformation or durability in “BIM-based construction clash detection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"模型能找出什麼碰撞，取決於模型發展程度（LOD）或資訊需求程度：LOD 300 的梁柱只有外形，看不到鋼筋、預埋件與鋼構接頭板，因此梁柱接頭的鋼筋擁擠、錨栓與套管衝突要到 LOD 350 或 400 的製造模型才會出現。BIMForum 的 LOD 規範依元素分類說明每個等級應包含的內容，專案應依協調目的指定每個階段需要的程度，而不是一律要求最高等級。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「鋼筋與預埋件密度」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"What clashes a model can reveal depends on its level of development or level of information need: LOD 300 beams and columns show only outer shape, without reinforcement, embeds or steel connection plates, so rebar congestion at beam–column joints and conflicts between anchors and sleeves only appear in LOD 350 or 400 fabrication models. The BIMForum LOD Specification describes what each level contains element by element, and a project should specify the level needed at each stage for its coordination purpose rather than demanding the highest level everywhere. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Rebar and embed congestion” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：梁寬 600 mm、保護層 40 mm、箍筋 13 mm、一層 8 支 32 mm 主筋：淨間距 = (600 − 2×40 − 2×13 − 8×32)/7 = 238/7 = 34.0 mm，大於 ACI 318 的下限 max(32 mm, 25 mm, 4/3×20 mm) = 32 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Beam width 600 mm, cover 40 mm, 13 mm stirrups and one layer of eight 32 mm bars: clear spacing = (600 − 2×40 − 2×13 − 8×32)/7 = 238/7 = 34.0 mm, above the ACI 318 minimum of max(32 mm, 25 mm, 4/3×20 mm) = 32 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有元素都要做到最高的模型發展程度，碰撞檢查才有意義。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every element must reach the highest level of development for clash detection to be meaningful.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「鋼筋與預埋件密度」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Rebar and embed congestion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-13-k1","title":"模型發展程度與細部碰撞","titleEn":"Level of development and detail clashes","text":"模型能找出什麼碰撞，取決於模型發展程度（LOD）或資訊需求程度：LOD 300 的梁柱只有外形，看不到鋼筋、預埋件與鋼構接頭板，因此梁柱接頭的鋼筋擁擠、錨栓與套管衝突要到 LOD 350 或 400 的製造模型才會出現。BIMForum 的 LOD 規範依元素分類說明每個等級應包含的內容，專案應依協調目的指定每個階段需要的程度，而不是一律要求最高等級。","textEn":"What clashes a model can reveal depends on its level of development or level of information need: LOD 300 beams and columns show only outer shape, without reinforcement, embeds or steel connection plates, so rebar congestion at beam–column joints and conflicts between anchors and sleeves only appear in LOD 350 or 400 fabrication models. The BIMForum LOD Specification describes what each level contains element by element, and a project should specify the level needed at each stage for its coordination purpose rather than demanding the highest level everywhere.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有元素都要做到最高的模型發展程度，碰撞檢查才有意義。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every element must reach the highest level of development for clash detection to be meaningful. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模型發展程度與細部碰撞」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Level of development and detail clashes\" is correct?","options":["所有元素都要做到最高的模型發展程度，碰撞檢查才有意義。","模型能找出什麼碰撞，取決於模型發展程度（LOD）或資訊需求程度：LOD 300 的梁柱只有外形，看不到鋼筋、預埋件與鋼構接頭板，因此梁柱接頭的鋼筋擁擠、錨栓與套管衝突要到 LOD 350 或 400 的製造模型才會出現。","碰撞報告產出後，軟體會自動決定哪個專業必須修改。"],"optionsEn":["Every element must reach the highest level of development for clash detection to be meaningful.","What clashes a model can reveal depends on its level of development or level of information need: LOD 300 beams and columns show only outer shape, without reinforcement, embeds or steel connection plates, so rebar congestion at beam–column joints and conflicts between anchors and sleeves only appear in LOD 350 or 400 fabrication models.","Once the clash report is produced, the software decides which discipline must change."],"answer":1,"explanation":"模型能找出什麼碰撞，取決於模型發展程度（LOD）或資訊需求程度：LOD 300 的梁柱只有外形，看不到鋼筋、預埋件與鋼構接頭板，因此梁柱接頭的鋼筋擁擠、錨栓與套管衝突要到 LOD 350 或 400 的製造模型才會出現。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"What clashes a model can reveal depends on its level of development or level of information need: LOD 300 beams and columns show only outer shape, without reinforcement, embeds or steel connection plates, so rebar congestion at beam–column joints and conflicts between anchors and sleeves only appear in LOD 350 or 400 fabrication models. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b096-v13-14","title":"模型發展程度與細部碰撞：定量估算","titleEn":"Level of development and detail clashes: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋼筋與預埋件密度」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rebar and embed congestion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：梁寬 600 mm、保護層 40 mm、箍筋 13 mm、一層 8 支 32 mm 主筋：淨間距 = (600 − 2×40 − 2×13 − 8×32)/7 = 238/7 = 34.0 mm，大於 ACI 318 的下限 max(32 mm, 25 mm, 4/3×20 mm) = 32 mm。若再加 1 支成 9 支：(494 − 288)/8 ≈ 25.8 mm，不合格。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Beam width 600 mm, cover 40 mm, 13 mm stirrups and one layer of eight 32 mm bars: clear spacing = (600 − 2×40 − 2×13 − 8×32)/7 = 238/7 = 34.0 mm, above the ACI 318 minimum of max(32 mm, 25 mm, 4/3×20 mm) = 32 mm. Adding a ninth bar gives (494 − 288)/8 ≈ 25.8 mm, which fails. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在梁柱接頭、轉換梁與機電套管密集區建立鋼筋與預埋件模型，以碰撞檢查找出鋼筋與套管、錨栓、預力管的衝突，再以淨間距規則檢查擁擠度；結果交由結構設計者確認，必要時以 1:1 樣品或局部模型試排。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Model reinforcement and embeds at beam–column joints, transfer beams and dense sleeve zones, run clash checks between bars and sleeves, anchors and post-tensioning ducts, then check congestion with clear-spacing rules; have the structural designer confirm the results and trial-place difficult joints with a full-size mock-up or local model when needed.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"梁寬 600 mm、保護層 40 mm、箍筋 13 mm、一層 8 支 32 mm 主筋：淨間距 = (600 − 2×40 − 2×13 − 8×32)/7 = 238/7 = 34.0 mm，大於 ACI 318 的下限 max(32 mm, 25 mm, 4/3×20 mm) = 32 mm。若再加 1 支成 9 支：(494 − 288)/8 ≈ 25.8 mm，不合格。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Beam width 600 mm, cover 40 mm, 13 mm stirrups and one layer of eight 32 mm bars: clear spacing = (600 − 2×40 − 2×13 − 8×32)/7 = 238/7 = 34.0 mm, above the ACI 318 minimum of max(32 mm, 25 mm, 4/3×20 mm) = 32 mm. Adding a ninth bar gives (494 − 288)/8 ≈ 25.8 mm, which fails. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「模型發展程度與細部碰撞」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Level of development and detail clashes\", which statement holds?","options":["碰撞數量越少，代表協調品質越好。","共用資料環境只是存放檔案的雲端資料夾。","梁寬 600 mm、保護層 40 mm、箍筋 13 mm、一層 8 支 32 mm 主筋：淨間距 = (600 − 2×40 − 2×13 − 8×32)/7 = 238/7 = 34.0 mm，大於 ACI 318 的下限 max(32 mm, 25 mm, 4/3×20 mm) = 32 mm。"],"optionsEn":["The fewer the clashes in the report, the better the coordination.","A common data environment is just a cloud folder for storing files.","Beam width 600 mm, cover 40 mm, 13 mm stirrups and one layer of eight 32 mm bars: clear spacing = (600 − 2×40 − 2×13 − 8×32)/7 = 238/7 = 34.0 mm, above the ACI 318 minimum of max(32 mm, 25 mm, 4/3×20 mm) = 32 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"梁寬 600 mm、保護層 40 mm、箍筋 13 mm、一層 8 支 32 mm 主筋：淨間距 = (600 − 2×40 − 2×13 − 8×32)/7 = 238/7 = 34.0 mm，大於 ACI 318 的下限 max(32 mm, 25 mm, 4/3×20 mm) = 32 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Beam width 600 mm, cover 40 mm, 13 mm stirrups and one layer of eight 32 mm bars: clear spacing = (600 − 2×40 − 2×13 − 8×32)/7 = 238/7 = 34.0 mm, above the ACI 318 minimum of max(32 mm, 25 mm, 4/3×20 mm) = 32 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b096-v13-15","title":"模型發展程度與細部碰撞：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Level of development and detail clashes: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋼筋與預埋件密度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rebar and embed congestion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在梁柱接頭、轉換梁與機電套管密集區建立鋼筋與預埋件模型，以碰撞檢查找出鋼筋與套管、錨栓、預力管的衝突，再以淨間距規則檢查擁擠度；結果交由結構設計者確認，必要時以 1:1 樣品或局部模型試排。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Model reinforcement and embeds at beam–column joints, transfer beams and dense sleeve zones, run clash checks between bars and sleeves, anchors and post-tensioning ducts, then check congestion with clear-spacing rules; have the structural designer confirm the results and trial-place difficult joints with a full-size mock-up or local model when needed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在資訊需求文件中依區域指定 LOD：一般樓板與牆面維持 LOD 300，鋼筋擁擠接頭、機電密集走廊與機房要求 LOD 350 至 400，並把這些高細度區域列為協調會議的固定議程。","observationEn":"Site practice: In the information requirements, assign LOD by area: keep typical slabs and walls at LOD 300, require LOD 350 to 400 for congested joints, dense service corridors and plant rooms, and make these high-detail areas a standing item on the coordination agenda.","failure":"注意干擾：只用外形模型做協調，報告看似乾淨，施工時卻發現接頭鋼筋與鋼骨柱的螺栓、灌漿管互相阻擋，混凝土無法填實而形成蜂窩；事後補強或改設計往往拖累整個樓層的工期。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Coordinating with shape-only models gives a clean-looking report, yet during construction joint bars block steel-column bolts and grout tubes so concrete cannot consolidate and honeycombs form; the subsequent repair or redesign often delays the whole floor cycle. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在梁柱接頭、轉換梁與機電套管密集區建立鋼筋與預埋件模型，以碰撞檢查找出鋼筋與套管、錨栓、預力管的衝突，再以淨間距規則檢查擁擠度；結果交由結構設計者確認，必要時以 1:1 樣品或局部模型試排。","textEn":"Model reinforcement and embeds at beam–column joints, transfer beams and dense sleeve zones, run clash checks between bars and sleeves, anchors and post-tensioning ducts, then check congestion with clear-spacing rules; have the structural designer confirm the results and trial-place difficult joints with a full-size mock-up or local model when needed.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在資訊需求文件中依區域指定 LOD：一般樓板與牆面維持 LOD 300，鋼筋擁擠接頭、機電密集走廊與機房要求 LOD 350 至 400，並把這些高細度區域列為協調會議的固定議程。","textEn":"In the information requirements, assign LOD by area: keep typical slabs and walls at LOD 300, require LOD 350 to 400 for congested joints, dense service corridors and plant rooms, and make these high-detail areas a standing item on the coordination agenda.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「模型發展程度與細部碰撞」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Level of development and detail clashes\"?","options":["在梁柱接頭、轉換梁與機電套管密集區建立鋼筋與預埋件模型，以碰撞檢查找出鋼筋與套管、錨栓、預力管的衝突，再以淨間距規則檢查擁擠度。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","碰撞檢查的主要目的是找建模錯誤，與樓高設計無關。"],"optionsEn":["Model reinforcement and embeds at beam–column joints, transfer beams and dense sleeve zones, run clash checks between bars and sleeves, anchors and post-tensioning ducts, then check congestion with clear-spacing rules.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Clash detection is mainly for catching modelling mistakes and has nothing to do with storey-height design."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在梁柱接頭、轉換梁與機電套管密集區建立鋼筋與預埋件模型，以碰撞檢查找出鋼筋與套管、錨栓、預力管的衝突，再以淨間距規則檢查擁擠度；結果交由結構設計者確認，必要時以 1:1 樣品或局部模型試排。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Model reinforcement and embeds at beam–column joints, transfer beams and dense sleeve zones, run clash checks between bars and sleeves, anchors and post-tensioning ducts, then check congestion with clear-spacing rules; have the structural designer confirm the results and trial-place difficult joints with a full-size mock-up or local model when needed. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b096-v13-16","title":"模型發展程度與細部碰撞：失效診斷","titleEn":"Level of development and detail clashes: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋼筋與預埋件密度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rebar and embed congestion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只用外形模型做協調，報告看似乾淨，施工時卻發現接頭鋼筋與鋼骨柱的螺栓、灌漿管互相阻擋，混凝土無法填實而形成蜂窩；事後補強或改設計往往拖累整個樓層的工期。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Coordinating with shape-only models gives a clean-looking report, yet during construction joint bars block steel-column bolts and grout tubes so concrete cannot consolidate and honeycombs form; the subsequent repair or redesign often delays the whole floor cycle. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：BIMForum 的 LOD 規範依元素分類說明每個等級應包含的內容，專案應依協調目的指定每個階段需要的程度，而不是一律要求最高等級。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The BIMForum LOD Specification describes what each level contains element by element, and a project should specify the level needed at each stage for its coordination purpose rather than demanding the highest level everywhere.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有元素都要做到最高的模型發展程度，碰撞檢查才有意義。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every element must reach the highest level of development for clash detection to be meaningful.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只用外形模型做協調，報告看似乾淨，施工時卻發現接頭鋼筋與鋼骨柱的螺栓、灌漿管互相阻擋，混凝土無法填實而形成蜂窩；事後補強或改設計往往拖累整個樓層的工期。","textEn":"Coordinating with shape-only models gives a clean-looking report, yet during construction joint bars block steel-column bolts and grout tubes so concrete cannot consolidate and honeycombs form; the subsequent repair or redesign often delays the whole floor cycle.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模型發展程度與細部碰撞」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Level of development and detail clashes\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只用外形模型做協調，報告看似乾淨，施工時卻發現接頭鋼筋與鋼骨柱的螺栓、灌漿管互相阻擋，混凝土無法填實而形成蜂窩；事後補強或改設計往往拖累整個樓層的工期。","碰撞報告產出後，軟體會自動決定哪個專業必須修改。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Coordinating with shape-only models gives a clean-looking report, yet during construction joint bars block steel-column bolts and grout tubes so concrete cannot consolidate and honeycombs form.","Once the clash report is produced, the software decides which discipline must change."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只用外形模型做協調，報告看似乾淨，施工時卻發現接頭鋼筋與鋼骨柱的螺栓、灌漿管互相阻擋，混凝土無法填實而形成蜂窩；事後補強或改設計往往拖累整個樓層的工期。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Coordinating with shape-only models gives a clean-looking report, yet during construction joint bars block steel-column bolts and grout tubes so concrete cannot consolidate and honeycombs form; the subsequent repair or redesign often delays the whole floor cycle. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b096-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「協調週期、議題追蹤與區域簽認」與「時空碰撞與施工順序模擬」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Coordination cycles, issue tracking and area sign-off\" and \"Space–time clashes and sequence simulation\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b096-v13-17","title":"協調週期、議題追蹤與區域簽認：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Coordination cycles, issue tracking and area sign-off: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「BCF 議題清單」如何影響工程數位模型碰撞檢查的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “BCF issue list” governs force, deformation or durability in “BIM-based construction clash detection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"碰撞檢查不是一次性的動作，而是每週或每兩週重複的協調循環：各專業上傳最新模型到共用資料環境，資訊管理者聯合模型並執行碰撞測試，把結果分組成議題，以 BCF 格式記錄視點、相關元素 GUID 與責任人，在協調會議中決定誰改、怎麼改，下一輪再確認是否關閉。某區域的議題清空並經各專業簽認後，才放行製造圖與預製。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「BCF 議題清單」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Clash detection is not a one-off act but a coordination cycle repeated weekly or fortnightly: each discipline uploads its latest model to the common data environment, the information manager federates and runs the tests, groups results into issues and records them in BCF with viewpoints, element GUIDs and owners, the coordination meeting decides who changes what, and the next round confirms closure. Only when an area's issues are cleared and signed off by every discipline are its fabrication drawings and prefabrication released. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “BCF issue list” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：議題數 N_k = N* + (N₀ − N*)(1−r)^k，穩態 N* = 每週新增/解決率。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Open issues N_k = N* + (N₀ − N*)(1−r)^k with steady state N* = new per week / resolution rate.","failure":"常見誤解：「碰撞報告產出後，軟體會自動決定哪個專業必須修改。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once the clash report is produced, the software decides which discipline must change.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「BCF 議題清單」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “BCF issue list”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-17-k1","title":"協調週期、議題追蹤與區域簽認","titleEn":"Coordination cycles, issue tracking and area sign-off","text":"碰撞檢查不是一次性的動作，而是每週或每兩週重複的協調循環：各專業上傳最新模型到共用資料環境，資訊管理者聯合模型並執行碰撞測試，把結果分組成議題，以 BCF 格式記錄視點、相關元素 GUID 與責任人，在協調會議中決定誰改、怎麼改，下一輪再確認是否關閉。某區域的議題清空並經各專業簽認後，才放行製造圖與預製。","textEn":"Clash detection is not a one-off act but a coordination cycle repeated weekly or fortnightly: each discipline uploads its latest model to the common data environment, the information manager federates and runs the tests, groups results into issues and records them in BCF with viewpoints, element GUIDs and owners, the coordination meeting decides who changes what, and the next round confirms closure. Only when an area's issues are cleared and signed off by every discipline are its fabrication drawings and prefabrication released.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：碰撞報告產出後，軟體會自動決定哪個專業必須修改。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once the clash report is produced, the software decides which discipline must change. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「協調週期、議題追蹤與區域簽認」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Coordination cycles, issue tracking and area sign-off\" is correct?","options":["碰撞報告產出後，軟體會自動決定哪個專業必須修改。","只要三維模型沒有碰撞，施工順序就不會發生衝突。","碰撞檢查不是一次性的動作，而是每週或每兩週重複的協調循環：各專業上傳最新模型到共用資料環境，資訊管理者聯合模型並執行碰撞測試，把結果分組成議題，以 BCF 格式記錄視點、相關元素 GUID 與責任人，在協調會議中決定誰改、怎麼改，下一輪再確認是否關閉。"],"optionsEn":["Once the clash report is produced, the software decides which discipline must change.","If the 3D model has no clashes, the construction sequence cannot conflict.","Clash detection is not a one-off act but a coordination cycle repeated weekly or fortnightly: each discipline uploads its latest model to the common data environment, the information manager federates and runs the tests, groups results into issues and records them in BCF with viewpoints, element GUIDs and owners, the coordination meeting decides who changes what, and the next round confirms closure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"碰撞檢查不是一次性的動作，而是每週或每兩週重複的協調循環：各專業上傳最新模型到共用資料環境，資訊管理者聯合模型並執行碰撞測試，把結果分組成議題，以 BCF 格式記錄視點、相關元素 GUID 與責任人，在協調會議中決定誰改、怎麼改，下一輪再確認是否關閉。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Clash detection is not a one-off act but a coordination cycle repeated weekly or fortnightly: each discipline uploads its latest model to the common data environment, the information manager federates and runs the tests, groups results into issues and records them in BCF with viewpoints, element GUIDs and owners, the coordination meeting decides who changes what, and the next round confirms closure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b096-v13-18","title":"協調週期、議題追蹤與區域簽認：定量估算","titleEn":"Coordination cycles, issue tracking and area sign-off: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「BCF 議題清單」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “BCF issue list” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：議題數 N_k = N* + (N₀ − N*)(1−r)^k，穩態 N* = 每週新增/解決率。取 N₀ = 600、每週解決 r = 35%、每週新增 40：N* = 40/0.35 ≈ 114。要降到 150 以下需 (600−114)×0.65^k ≤ 36，即 0.65^k ≤ 0.074，k ≥ ln 0.074/ln 0.65 ≈ 6.04，取 7 週。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Open issues N_k = N* + (N₀ − N*)(1−r)^k with steady state N* = new per week / resolution rate. With N₀ = 600, r = 35% per week and 40 new issues per week: N* = 40/0.35 ≈ 114. Falling below 150 needs (600−114)×0.65^k ≤ 36, so 0.65^k ≤ 0.074 and k ≥ ln 0.074/ln 0.65 ≈ 6.04, giving 7 weeks. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以 BCF 或議題追蹤平台統計每週新增、關閉與逾期議題，畫出每個區域的燃盡曲線並與製造圖送審時程對照；區域簽認表需有各專業負責人簽名與模型版本號，監造抽查已簽認區域是否確實沒有未關閉議題。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Count new, closed and overdue issues each week in BCF or the issue platform, plot a burn-down for every area against the fabrication-drawing schedule, and require each area sign-off sheet to carry the signatures of all discipline leads and the model revision numbers; the supervising engineer spot-checks that signed-off areas really have no open issues.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"議題數 N_k = N* + (N₀ − N*)(1−r)^k，穩態 N* = 每週新增/解決率。取 N₀ = 600、每週解決 r = 35%、每週新增 40：N* = 40/0.35 ≈ 114。要降到 150 以下需 (600−114)×0.65^k ≤ 36，即 0.65^k ≤ 0.074，k ≥ ln 0.074/ln 0.65 ≈ 6.04，取 7 週。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Open issues N_k = N* + (N₀ − N*)(1−r)^k with steady state N* = new per week / resolution rate. With N₀ = 600, r = 35% per week and 40 new issues per week: N* = 40/0.35 ≈ 114. Falling below 150 needs (600−114)×0.65^k ≤ 36, so 0.65^k ≤ 0.074 and k ≥ ln 0.074/ln 0.65 ≈ 6.04, giving 7 weeks. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「協調週期、議題追蹤與區域簽認」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Coordination cycles, issue tracking and area sign-off\", which statement holds?","options":["議題數 N_k = N* + (N₀ − N*)(1−r)^k，穩態 N* = 每週新增/解決率。","模型協調完成後，現場只要照圖施工就不會有空間衝突。","施工期間協調用的模型就等於竣工模型。"],"optionsEn":["Open issues N_k = N* + (N₀ − N*)(1−r)^k with steady state N* = new per week / resolution rate.","Once the model is coordinated, building to the drawings cannot produce space conflicts.","The model used for coordination during construction is the as-built model."],"answer":0,"explanation":"議題數 N_k = N* + (N₀ − N*)(1−r)^k，穩態 N* = 每週新增/解決率。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Open issues N_k = N* + (N₀ − N*)(1−r)^k with steady state N* = new per week / resolution rate. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b096-v13-19","title":"協調週期、議題追蹤與區域簽認：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Coordination cycles, issue tracking and area sign-off: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「BCF 議題清單」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “BCF issue list” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以 BCF 或議題追蹤平台統計每週新增、關閉與逾期議題，畫出每個區域的燃盡曲線並與製造圖送審時程對照；區域簽認表需有各專業負責人簽名與模型版本號，監造抽查已簽認區域是否確實沒有未關閉議題。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Count new, closed and overdue issues each week in BCF or the issue platform, plot a burn-down for every area against the fabrication-drawing schedule, and require each area sign-off sheet to carry the signatures of all discipline leads and the model revision numbers; the supervising engineer spot-checks that signed-off areas really have no open issues. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以區域簽認作為預製放行的保留點：未經建築、結構、機電與消防負責人簽認的區域，不得發出製造圖或材料訂單；每個議題都要有單一責任人與到期日。","observationEn":"Site practice: Make area sign-off the hold point for releasing prefabrication: no fabrication drawings or material orders may be issued for an area until the architecture, structure, MEP and fire leads have signed it off, and every issue has a single owner and a due date.","failure":"注意干擾：協調會議只播放碰撞畫面而沒有指定責任人與期限，議題數長期停在高檔；製造廠在區域未簽認前就依舊模型預製風管與管架，到現場才發現已改線，整批材料報廢。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Meetings that only replay clash views without naming owners and deadlines leave issue counts high for months; a fabricator that prefabricates ducts and racks from an old model before area sign-off finds on site that routes have changed and scraps the whole batch. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以 BCF 或議題追蹤平台統計每週新增、關閉與逾期議題，畫出每個區域的燃盡曲線並與製造圖送審時程對照；區域簽認表需有各專業負責人簽名與模型版本號，監造抽查已簽認區域是否確實沒有未關閉議題。","textEn":"Count new, closed and overdue issues each week in BCF or the issue platform, plot a burn-down for every area against the fabrication-drawing schedule, and require each area sign-off sheet to carry the signatures of all discipline leads and the model revision numbers; the supervising engineer spot-checks that signed-off areas really have no open issues.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以區域簽認作為預製放行的保留點：未經建築、結構、機電與消防負責人簽認的區域，不得發出製造圖或材料訂單；每個議題都要有單一責任人與到期日。","textEn":"Make area sign-off the hold point for releasing prefabrication: no fabrication drawings or material orders may be issued for an area until the architecture, structure, MEP and fire leads have signed it off, and every issue has a single owner and a due date.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「協調週期、議題追蹤與區域簽認」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Coordination cycles, issue tracking and area sign-off\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以 BCF 或議題追蹤平台統計每週新增、關閉與逾期議題，畫出每個區域的燃盡曲線並與製造圖送審時程對照。","只要把所有檔案匯入同一個軟體，模型就會自動對齊。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Count new, closed and overdue issues each week in BCF or the issue platform, plot a burn-down for every area against the fabrication-drawing schedule, and require each area sign-off sheet to carry the signatures of all discipline leads and the model revision numbers.","Importing every file into the same software aligns the models automatically."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以 BCF 或議題追蹤平台統計每週新增、關閉與逾期議題，畫出每個區域的燃盡曲線並與製造圖送審時程對照；區域簽認表需有各專業負責人簽名與模型版本號，監造抽查已簽認區域是否確實沒有未關閉議題。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Count new, closed and overdue issues each week in BCF or the issue platform, plot a burn-down for every area against the fabrication-drawing schedule, and require each area sign-off sheet to carry the signatures of all discipline leads and the model revision numbers; the supervising engineer spot-checks that signed-off areas really have no open issues. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b096-v13-20","title":"協調週期、議題追蹤與區域簽認：失效診斷","titleEn":"Coordination cycles, issue tracking and area sign-off: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「BCF 議題清單」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “BCF issue list” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"協調會議只播放碰撞畫面而沒有指定責任人與期限，議題數長期停在高檔；製造廠在區域未簽認前就依舊模型預製風管與管架，到現場才發現已改線，整批材料報廢。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Meetings that only replay clash views without naming owners and deadlines leave issue counts high for months; a fabricator that prefabricates ducts and racks from an old model before area sign-off finds on site that routes have changed and scraps the whole batch. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：某區域的議題清空並經各專業簽認後，才放行製造圖與預製。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Only when an area's issues are cleared and signed off by every discipline are its fabrication drawings and prefabrication released.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「碰撞報告產出後，軟體會自動決定哪個專業必須修改。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once the clash report is produced, the software decides which discipline must change.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"協調會議只播放碰撞畫面而沒有指定責任人與期限，議題數長期停在高檔；製造廠在區域未簽認前就依舊模型預製風管與管架，到現場才發現已改線，整批材料報廢。","textEn":"Meetings that only replay clash views without naming owners and deadlines leave issue counts high for months; a fabricator that prefabricates ducts and racks from an old model before area sign-off finds on site that routes have changed and scraps the whole batch.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「協調週期、議題追蹤與區域簽認」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Coordination cycles, issue tracking and area sign-off\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","只要三維模型沒有碰撞，施工順序就不會發生衝突。","協調會議只播放碰撞畫面而沒有指定責任人與期限，議題數長期停在高檔；製造廠在區域未簽認前就依舊模型預製風管與管架，到現場才發現已改線，整批材料報廢。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","If the 3D model has no clashes, the construction sequence cannot conflict.","Meetings that only replay clash views without naming owners and deadlines leave issue counts high for months."],"answer":2,"explanation":"協調會議只播放碰撞畫面而沒有指定責任人與期限，議題數長期停在高檔；製造廠在區域未簽認前就依舊模型預製風管與管架，到現場才發現已改線，整批材料報廢。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Meetings that only replay clash views without naming owners and deadlines leave issue counts high for months; a fabricator that prefabricates ducts and racks from an old model before area sign-off finds on site that routes have changed and scraps the whole batch. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b096-v13-21","title":"時空碰撞與施工順序模擬：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Space–time clashes and sequence simulation: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「4D 施工順序」如何影響工程數位模型碰撞檢查的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “4D construction sequence” governs force, deformation or durability in “BIM-based construction clash detection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"空間沒有碰撞，不代表施工可行：兩組工班若在同一時間需要同一區域，或塔吊吊運路徑穿過正在組立的支撐架，都是時空碰撞。4D 模型把模型元素與排程活動連結，依時間播放施工順序，並可加入工作空間、吊裝範圍與臨時結構，檢查同一時段是否有空間重疊。Crossrail 在法靈頓站以約 12 萬英鎊做 3D 排程分析，促成約 800 萬英鎊風險預備金的釋出，顯示排程協調的價值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「4D 施工順序」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A model without spatial clashes is not necessarily buildable: two crews needing the same area at once, or a tower-crane lift path crossing temporary shoring under erection, are space–time clashes. A 4D model links model elements to schedule activities, plays the construction sequence over time and can include workspaces, lifting zones and temporary works to detect overlaps in the same period. At Farringdon station Crossrail spent about £120k on 3D schedule analysis, which enabled about £8 million of risk contingency to be released, showing the value of schedule coordination. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “4D construction sequence” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：第 3 區的風管安裝排在第 10 至 18 天，天花板骨架排在第 16 至 22 天，兩者在第 16、17、18 天重疊，共 3 天。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: In zone 3, duct installation runs on days 10 to 18 and ceiling framing on days 16 to 22, overlapping on days 16, 17 and 18, three days in all.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要三維模型沒有碰撞，施工順序就不會發生衝突。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the 3D model has no clashes, the construction sequence cannot conflict.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「4D 施工順序」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “4D construction sequence”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-21-k1","title":"時空碰撞與施工順序模擬","titleEn":"Space–time clashes and sequence simulation","text":"空間沒有碰撞，不代表施工可行：兩組工班若在同一時間需要同一區域，或塔吊吊運路徑穿過正在組立的支撐架，都是時空碰撞。4D 模型把模型元素與排程活動連結，依時間播放施工順序，並可加入工作空間、吊裝範圍與臨時結構，檢查同一時段是否有空間重疊。","textEn":"A model without spatial clashes is not necessarily buildable: two crews needing the same area at once, or a tower-crane lift path crossing temporary shoring under erection, are space–time clashes. A 4D model links model elements to schedule activities, plays the construction sequence over time and can include workspaces, lifting zones and temporary works to detect overlaps in the same period.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要三維模型沒有碰撞，施工順序就不會發生衝突。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the 3D model has no clashes, the construction sequence cannot conflict. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「時空碰撞與施工順序模擬」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Space–time clashes and sequence simulation\" is correct?","options":["空間沒有碰撞，不代表施工可行：兩組工班若在同一時間需要同一區域，或塔吊吊運路徑穿過正在組立的支撐架，都是時空碰撞。","只要三維模型沒有碰撞，施工順序就不會發生衝突。","碰撞數量越少，代表協調品質越好。"],"optionsEn":["A model without spatial clashes is not necessarily buildable: two crews needing the same area at once, or a tower-crane lift path crossing temporary shoring under erection, are space–time clashes.","If the 3D model has no clashes, the construction sequence cannot conflict.","The fewer the clashes in the report, the better the coordination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"空間沒有碰撞，不代表施工可行：兩組工班若在同一時間需要同一區域，或塔吊吊運路徑穿過正在組立的支撐架，都是時空碰撞。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A model without spatial clashes is not necessarily buildable: two crews needing the same area at once, or a tower-crane lift path crossing temporary shoring under erection, are space–time clashes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b096-v13-22","title":"時空碰撞與施工順序模擬：定量估算","titleEn":"Space–time clashes and sequence simulation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「4D 施工順序」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “4D construction sequence” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：第 3 區的風管安裝排在第 10 至 18 天，天花板骨架排在第 16 至 22 天，兩者在第 16、17、18 天重疊，共 3 天。若天花板活動的總浮時只有 2 天，延後 3 天會使完工日延後 3 − 2 = 1 天；改把第 3 區分成 3a、3b 兩段交錯施工即可消除重疊。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: In zone 3, duct installation runs on days 10 to 18 and ceiling framing on days 16 to 22, overlapping on days 16, 17 and 18, three days in all. If the ceiling activity has only 2 days of total float, delaying it by 3 days pushes completion by 3 − 2 = 1 day; splitting zone 3 into 3a and 3b and staggering the work removes the overlap. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以 4D 模擬逐週檢查工作空間、吊裝範圍、臨時支撐與材料堆置是否重疊，並與總承包商的三週滾動計畫比對；每月以現場照片或掃描檢查實際進度與 4D 模型是否一致，偏離時更新排程後重新模擬。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use 4D simulation to check weekly for overlaps between workspaces, lifting zones, temporary supports and laydown areas, compare it with the main contractor's three-week look-ahead, and each month compare site photographs or scans with the 4D model, updating the schedule and re-simulating when they diverge.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"第 3 區的風管安裝排在第 10 至 18 天，天花板骨架排在第 16 至 22 天，兩者在第 16、17、18 天重疊，共 3 天。若天花板活動的總浮時只有 2 天，延後 3 天會使完工日延後 3 − 2 = 1 天；改把第 3 區分成 3a、3b 兩段交錯施工即可消除重疊。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"In zone 3, duct installation runs on days 10 to 18 and ceiling framing on days 16 to 22, overlapping on days 16, 17 and 18, three days in all. If the ceiling activity has only 2 days of total float, delaying it by 3 days pushes completion by 3 − 2 = 1 day; splitting zone 3 into 3a and 3b and staggering the work removes the overlap. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「時空碰撞與施工順序模擬」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Space–time clashes and sequence simulation\", which statement holds?","options":["共用資料環境只是存放檔案的雲端資料夾。","第 3 區的風管安裝排在第 10 至 18 天，天花板骨架排在第 16 至 22 天，兩者在第 16、17、18 天重疊，共 3 天。","碰撞檢查的主要目的是找建模錯誤，與樓高設計無關。"],"optionsEn":["A common data environment is just a cloud folder for storing files.","In zone 3, duct installation runs on days 10 to 18 and ceiling framing on days 16 to 22, overlapping on days 16, 17 and 18, three days in all.","Clash detection is mainly for catching modelling mistakes and has nothing to do with storey-height design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"第 3 區的風管安裝排在第 10 至 18 天，天花板骨架排在第 16 至 22 天，兩者在第 16、17、18 天重疊，共 3 天。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"In zone 3, duct installation runs on days 10 to 18 and ceiling framing on days 16 to 22, overlapping on days 16, 17 and 18, three days in all. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b096-v13-23","title":"時空碰撞與施工順序模擬：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Space–time clashes and sequence simulation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「4D 施工順序」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “4D construction sequence” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以 4D 模擬逐週檢查工作空間、吊裝範圍、臨時支撐與材料堆置是否重疊，並與總承包商的三週滾動計畫比對；每月以現場照片或掃描檢查實際進度與 4D 模型是否一致，偏離時更新排程後重新模擬。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use 4D simulation to check weekly for overlaps between workspaces, lifting zones, temporary supports and laydown areas, compare it with the main contractor's three-week look-ahead, and each month compare site photographs or scans with the 4D model, updating the schedule and re-simulating when they diverge. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：大型設備吊入路徑、臨時開口與吊裝區應建成模型物件並納入碰撞矩陣，其封閉時點列入排程；吊裝計畫本身仍須由合格吊掛工程師與工地主任依規定核准，4D 模擬只是協調工具。","observationEn":"Site practice: Model large-equipment lift routes, temporary openings and lifting zones as objects in the clash matrix and put their closing dates in the schedule; the lifting plan itself must still be approved by a qualified lifting engineer and the site manager as the rules require, with 4D simulation serving only as a coordination tool.","failure":"注意干擾：只檢查永久構件的空間碰撞而忽略臨時支撐與吊運路徑，結果大型機電模組無法從預留開口吊入，因為開口已被先施工的管線佔用，只好拆除部分已完成工作再吊裝。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Checking only permanent elements and ignoring temporary supports and lifting routes can mean a large MEP module cannot be lifted in through its reserved opening because services installed earlier now occupy it, so finished work must be partly removed to make the lift. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以 4D 模擬逐週檢查工作空間、吊裝範圍、臨時支撐與材料堆置是否重疊，並與總承包商的三週滾動計畫比對；每月以現場照片或掃描檢查實際進度與 4D 模型是否一致，偏離時更新排程後重新模擬。","textEn":"Use 4D simulation to check weekly for overlaps between workspaces, lifting zones, temporary supports and laydown areas, compare it with the main contractor's three-week look-ahead, and each month compare site photographs or scans with the 4D model, updating the schedule and re-simulating when they diverge.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"大型設備吊入路徑、臨時開口與吊裝區應建成模型物件並納入碰撞矩陣，其封閉時點列入排程；吊裝計畫本身仍須由合格吊掛工程師與工地主任依規定核准，4D 模擬只是協調工具。","textEn":"Model large-equipment lift routes, temporary openings and lifting zones as objects in the clash matrix and put their closing dates in the schedule; the lifting plan itself must still be approved by a qualified lifting engineer and the site manager as the rules require, with 4D simulation serving only as a coordination tool.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「時空碰撞與施工順序模擬」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Space–time clashes and sequence simulation\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","碰撞報告為零，就代表現場一定可以順利安裝。","以 4D 模擬逐週檢查工作空間、吊裝範圍、臨時支撐與材料堆置是否重疊，並與總承包商的三週滾動計畫比對。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A clash report of zero guarantees smooth installation on site.","Use 4D simulation to check weekly for overlaps between workspaces, lifting zones, temporary supports and laydown areas, compare it with the main contractor's three-week look-ahead, and each month compare site photographs or scans with the 4D model, updating the schedule and re-simulating when they diverge."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以 4D 模擬逐週檢查工作空間、吊裝範圍、臨時支撐與材料堆置是否重疊，並與總承包商的三週滾動計畫比對；每月以現場照片或掃描檢查實際進度與 4D 模型是否一致，偏離時更新排程後重新模擬。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use 4D simulation to check weekly for overlaps between workspaces, lifting zones, temporary supports and laydown areas, compare it with the main contractor's three-week look-ahead, and each month compare site photographs or scans with the 4D model, updating the schedule and re-simulating when they diverge. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b096-v13-24","title":"時空碰撞與施工順序模擬：失效診斷","titleEn":"Space–time clashes and sequence simulation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「4D 施工順序」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “4D construction sequence” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只檢查永久構件的空間碰撞而忽略臨時支撐與吊運路徑，結果大型機電模組無法從預留開口吊入，因為開口已被先施工的管線佔用，只好拆除部分已完成工作再吊裝。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Checking only permanent elements and ignoring temporary supports and lifting routes can mean a large MEP module cannot be lifted in through its reserved opening because services installed earlier now occupy it, so finished work must be partly removed to make the lift. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：Crossrail 在法靈頓站以約 12 萬英鎊做 3D 排程分析，促成約 800 萬英鎊風險預備金的釋出，顯示排程協調的價值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: At Farringdon station Crossrail spent about £120k on 3D schedule analysis, which enabled about £8 million of risk contingency to be released, showing the value of schedule coordination.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要三維模型沒有碰撞，施工順序就不會發生衝突。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the 3D model has no clashes, the construction sequence cannot conflict.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只檢查永久構件的空間碰撞而忽略臨時支撐與吊運路徑，結果大型機電模組無法從預留開口吊入，因為開口已被先施工的管線佔用，只好拆除部分已完成工作再吊裝。","textEn":"Checking only permanent elements and ignoring temporary supports and lifting routes can mean a large MEP module cannot be lifted in through its reserved opening because services installed earlier now occupy it, so finished work must be partly removed to make the lift.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「時空碰撞與施工順序模擬」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Space–time clashes and sequence simulation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只檢查永久構件的空間碰撞而忽略臨時支撐與吊運路徑，結果大型機電模組無法從預留開口吊入，因為開口已被先施工的管線佔用，只好拆除部分已完成工作再吊裝。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","碰撞數量越少，代表協調品質越好。"],"optionsEn":["Checking only permanent elements and ignoring temporary supports and lifting routes can mean a large MEP module cannot be lifted in through its reserved opening because services installed earlier now occupy it, so finished work must be partly removed to make the lift.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","The fewer the clashes in the report, the better the coordination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只檢查永久構件的空間碰撞而忽略臨時支撐與吊運路徑，結果大型機電模組無法從預留開口吊入，因為開口已被先施工的管線佔用，只好拆除部分已完成工作再吊裝。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Checking only permanent elements and ignoring temporary supports and lifting routes can mean a large MEP module cannot be lifted in through its reserved opening because services installed earlier now occupy it, so finished work must be partly removed to make the lift. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b096-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「碰撞分組、誤報與模型品質」與「現場安裝公差與模型驗證」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Clash grouping, false positives and model quality\" and \"Installation tolerances and field verification of the model\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b096-v13-25","title":"碰撞分組、誤報與模型品質：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Clash grouping, false positives and model quality: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「規則式模型檢查」如何影響工程數位模型碰撞檢查的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rule-based model checking” governs force, deformation or durability in “BIM-based construction clash detection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"原始碰撞報告常有數千至上萬筆結果，其中大部分是同一原因重複出現，例如一根風管穿過二十根吊桿就產生二十筆。有效的審查先依元素、系統、樓層或格線分組，排除建模雜訊，再由人判斷哪些是需要設計決策的真實議題。碰撞檢查只看幾何，因此還要以規則式模型檢查補足：重複元素、未連接的管線、缺少系統分類或防火等級屬性，都會讓碰撞結果失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「規則式模型檢查」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Raw clash reports often contain thousands to tens of thousands of results, most of them repeats of one cause; one duct passing twenty hanger rods produces twenty results. Effective review first groups results by element, system, level or grid, removes modelling noise, and then lets people judge which are real issues needing design decisions. Clash detection sees only geometry, so rule-based model checking must complement it: duplicate elements, unconnected pipework and missing system or fire-rating properties all distort clash results. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Rule-based model checking” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原始結果 12,000 筆，依元素與區域分組成 480 組，審查確認其中 120 組為真實設計議題：以組計的精確率 120/480 = 25%，以原始筆數計僅 120/12,000 = 1%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: 12,000 raw results grouped by element and zone become 480 groups, of which review confirms 120 as real design issues: precision is 120/480 = 25% by group but only 120/12,000 = 1% by raw result.","failure":"常見誤解：「碰撞數量越少，代表協調品質越好。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The fewer the clashes in the report, the better the coordination.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「規則式模型檢查」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Rule-based model checking”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-25-k1","title":"碰撞分組、誤報與模型品質","titleEn":"Clash grouping, false positives and model quality","text":"原始碰撞報告常有數千至上萬筆結果，其中大部分是同一原因重複出現，例如一根風管穿過二十根吊桿就產生二十筆。有效的審查先依元素、系統、樓層或格線分組，排除建模雜訊，再由人判斷哪些是需要設計決策的真實議題。","textEn":"Raw clash reports often contain thousands to tens of thousands of results, most of them repeats of one cause; one duct passing twenty hanger rods produces twenty results. Effective review first groups results by element, system, level or grid, removes modelling noise, and then lets people judge which are real issues needing design decisions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：碰撞數量越少，代表協調品質越好。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The fewer the clashes in the report, the better the coordination. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「碰撞分組、誤報與模型品質」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Clash grouping, false positives and model quality\" is correct?","options":["碰撞數量越少，代表協調品質越好。","原始碰撞報告常有數千至上萬筆結果，其中大部分是同一原因重複出現，例如一根風管穿過二十根吊桿就產生二十筆。","模型協調完成後，現場只要照圖施工就不會有空間衝突。"],"optionsEn":["The fewer the clashes in the report, the better the coordination.","Raw clash reports often contain thousands to tens of thousands of results, most of them repeats of one cause.","Once the model is coordinated, building to the drawings cannot produce space conflicts."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原始碰撞報告常有數千至上萬筆結果，其中大部分是同一原因重複出現，例如一根風管穿過二十根吊桿就產生二十筆。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Raw clash reports often contain thousands to tens of thousands of results, most of them repeats of one cause; one duct passing twenty hanger rods produces twenty results. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b096-v13-26","title":"碰撞分組、誤報與模型品質：定量估算","titleEn":"Clash grouping, false positives and model quality: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「規則式模型檢查」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rule-based model checking” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原始結果 12,000 筆，依元素與區域分組成 480 組，審查確認其中 120 組為真實設計議題：以組計的精確率 120/480 = 25%，以原始筆數計僅 120/12,000 = 1%。每組審查 6 分鐘約需 480×6/60 = 48 小時；逐筆每筆 0.5 分鐘則需 12,000×0.5/60 = 100 小時。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: 12,000 raw results grouped by element and zone become 480 groups, of which review confirms 120 as real design issues: precision is 120/480 = 25% by group but only 120/12,000 = 1% by raw result. At 6 minutes per group, review takes 480×6/60 = 48 hours; reviewing raw results at 0.5 minutes each would take 12,000×0.5/60 = 100 hours. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每次聯合前先執行規則式模型檢查（重複物件、空間未封閉、缺屬性、不合理尺寸），通過門檻（例如失敗元素少於 1%）才進入碰撞測試；分組規則與排除清單要版本化，並抽查被排除的結果，確認沒有誤刪真實問題。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before each federation run rule-based model checks (duplicates, unclosed spaces, missing properties, implausible sizes) and allow clash testing only above a threshold such as fewer than 1% failing elements; version the grouping rules and exclusion lists and spot-check excluded results to confirm that no real problem was discarded.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原始結果 12,000 筆，依元素與區域分組成 480 組，審查確認其中 120 組為真實設計議題：以組計的精確率 120/480 = 25%，以原始筆數計僅 120/12,000 = 1%。每組審查 6 分鐘約需 480×6/60 = 48 小時；逐筆每筆 0.5 分鐘則需 12,000×0.5/60 = 100 小時。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"12,000 raw results grouped by element and zone become 480 groups, of which review confirms 120 as real design issues: precision is 120/480 = 25% by group but only 120/12,000 = 1% by raw result. At 6 minutes per group, review takes 480×6/60 = 48 hours; reviewing raw results at 0.5 minutes each would take 12,000×0.5/60 = 100 hours. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「碰撞分組、誤報與模型品質」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Clash grouping, false positives and model quality\", which statement holds?","options":["施工期間協調用的模型就等於竣工模型。","只要把所有檔案匯入同一個軟體，模型就會自動對齊。","原始結果 12,000 筆，依元素與區域分組成 480 組，審查確認其中 120 組為真實設計議題：以組計的精確率 120/480 = 25%，以原始筆數計僅 120/12,000 = 1%。"],"optionsEn":["The model used for coordination during construction is the as-built model.","Importing every file into the same software aligns the models automatically.","12,000 raw results grouped by element and zone become 480 groups, of which review confirms 120 as real design issues: precision is 120/480 = 25% by group but only 120/12,000 = 1% by raw result."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原始結果 12,000 筆，依元素與區域分組成 480 組，審查確認其中 120 組為真實設計議題：以組計的精確率 120/480 = 25%，以原始筆數計僅 120/12,000 = 1%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"12,000 raw results grouped by element and zone become 480 groups, of which review confirms 120 as real design issues: precision is 120/480 = 25% by group but only 120/12,000 = 1% by raw result. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b096-v13-27","title":"碰撞分組、誤報與模型品質：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Clash grouping, false positives and model quality: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「規則式模型檢查」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rule-based model checking” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每次聯合前先執行規則式模型檢查（重複物件、空間未封閉、缺屬性、不合理尺寸），通過門檻（例如失敗元素少於 1%）才進入碰撞測試；分組規則與排除清單要版本化，並抽查被排除的結果，確認沒有誤刪真實問題。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before each federation run rule-based model checks (duplicates, unclosed spaces, missing properties, implausible sizes) and allow clash testing only above a threshold such as fewer than 1% failing elements; version the grouping rules and exclusion lists and spot-check excluded results to confirm that no real problem was discarded. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：協調報表應同時呈現原始數、分組數、真實議題數與逾期數，由不參與建模的協調經理抽查排除與核可紀錄；任何「核可碰撞」都要寫明理由與核可人。","observationEn":"Site practice: Coordination reports should show raw counts, groups, real issues and overdue issues together, with a coordination manager who does not model spot-checking exclusions and approvals; every ‘approved clash’ must record its reason and approver.","failure":"注意干擾：團隊為了讓數字好看而大量標記「已核可」或擴大排除條件，管理報表顯示碰撞快速下降，真正的衝突卻被埋進排除清單，直到現場安裝才暴露。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Teams that mark results ‘approved’ en masse or widen exclusions to make numbers look good see management reports show clashes falling fast, while real conflicts are buried in exclusion lists until site installation exposes them. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每次聯合前先執行規則式模型檢查（重複物件、空間未封閉、缺屬性、不合理尺寸），通過門檻（例如失敗元素少於 1%）才進入碰撞測試；分組規則與排除清單要版本化，並抽查被排除的結果，確認沒有誤刪真實問題。","textEn":"Before each federation run rule-based model checks (duplicates, unclosed spaces, missing properties, implausible sizes) and allow clash testing only above a threshold such as fewer than 1% failing elements; version the grouping rules and exclusion lists and spot-check excluded results to confirm that no real problem was discarded.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"協調報表應同時呈現原始數、分組數、真實議題數與逾期數，由不參與建模的協調經理抽查排除與核可紀錄；任何「核可碰撞」都要寫明理由與核可人。","textEn":"Coordination reports should show raw counts, groups, real issues and overdue issues together, with a coordination manager who does not model spot-checking exclusions and approvals; every ‘approved clash’ must record its reason and approver.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「碰撞分組、誤報與模型品質」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Clash grouping, false positives and model quality\"?","options":["每次聯合前先執行規則式模型檢查（重複物件、空間未封閉、缺屬性、不合理尺寸），通過門檻（例如失敗元素少於 1%）才進入碰撞測試。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","所有元素都要做到最高的模型發展程度，碰撞檢查才有意義。"],"optionsEn":["Before each federation run rule-based model checks (duplicates, unclosed spaces, missing properties, implausible sizes) and allow clash testing only above a threshold such as fewer than 1% failing elements.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Every element must reach the highest level of development for clash detection to be meaningful."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每次聯合前先執行規則式模型檢查（重複物件、空間未封閉、缺屬性、不合理尺寸），通過門檻（例如失敗元素少於 1%）才進入碰撞測試；分組規則與排除清單要版本化，並抽查被排除的結果，確認沒有誤刪真實問題。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before each federation run rule-based model checks (duplicates, unclosed spaces, missing properties, implausible sizes) and allow clash testing only above a threshold such as fewer than 1% failing elements; version the grouping rules and exclusion lists and spot-check excluded results to confirm that no real problem was discarded. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b096-v13-28","title":"碰撞分組、誤報與模型品質：失效診斷","titleEn":"Clash grouping, false positives and model quality: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「規則式模型檢查」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rule-based model checking” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"團隊為了讓數字好看而大量標記「已核可」或擴大排除條件，管理報表顯示碰撞快速下降，真正的衝突卻被埋進排除清單，直到現場安裝才暴露。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Teams that mark results ‘approved’ en masse or widen exclusions to make numbers look good see management reports show clashes falling fast, while real conflicts are buried in exclusion lists until site installation exposes them. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：碰撞檢查只看幾何，因此還要以規則式模型檢查補足：重複元素、未連接的管線、缺少系統分類或防火等級屬性，都會讓碰撞結果失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Clash detection sees only geometry, so rule-based model checking must complement it: duplicate elements, unconnected pipework and missing system or fire-rating properties all distort clash results.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「碰撞數量越少，代表協調品質越好。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The fewer the clashes in the report, the better the coordination.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"團隊為了讓數字好看而大量標記「已核可」或擴大排除條件，管理報表顯示碰撞快速下降，真正的衝突卻被埋進排除清單，直到現場安裝才暴露。","textEn":"Teams that mark results ‘approved’ en masse or widen exclusions to make numbers look good see management reports show clashes falling fast, while real conflicts are buried in exclusion lists until site installation exposes them.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「碰撞分組、誤報與模型品質」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Clash grouping, false positives and model quality\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","團隊為了讓數字好看而大量標記「已核可」或擴大排除條件，管理報表顯示碰撞快速下降，真正的衝突卻被埋進排除清單，直到現場安裝才暴露。","模型協調完成後，現場只要照圖施工就不會有空間衝突。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Teams that mark results ‘approved’ en masse or widen exclusions to make numbers look good see management reports show clashes falling fast, while real conflicts are buried in exclusion lists until site installation exposes them.","Once the model is coordinated, building to the drawings cannot produce space conflicts."],"answer":1,"explanation":"團隊為了讓數字好看而大量標記「已核可」或擴大排除條件，管理報表顯示碰撞快速下降，真正的衝突卻被埋進排除清單，直到現場安裝才暴露。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Teams that mark results ‘approved’ en masse or widen exclusions to make numbers look good see management reports show clashes falling fast, while real conflicts are buried in exclusion lists until site installation exposes them. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b096-v13-29","title":"現場安裝公差與模型驗證：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Installation tolerances and field verification of the model: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「現場放樣與公差累積」如何影響工程數位模型碰撞檢查的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Site set-out and tolerance stack” governs force, deformation or durability in “BIM-based construction clash detection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"模型中相距幾公釐的兩個物件，在現場可能因放樣、預製尺寸與安裝誤差而相撞。因此協調後的模型要經由全測站或雷射掃描回到現場：先以模型座標放樣吊架與套管位置，安裝後再量測實際位置與模型比對。這一步把虛擬協調與實體施工連成閉環，也讓軟碰撞淨距有了依據：淨距應涵蓋各項誤差的合成，而不是任意的數字。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「現場放樣與公差累積」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Two objects a few millimetres apart in the model can collide on site because of set-out, fabrication and installation errors. The coordinated model must therefore return to site through total stations or laser scanning: hangers and sleeves are set out from model coordinates, and after installation actual positions are measured and compared with the model. This closes the loop between virtual coordination and physical construction and gives the clearance rules a basis, since the clearance should cover the combined errors rather than an arbitrary number. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Site set-out and tolerance stack” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：單一物件位置誤差以平方和開根號合成：放樣 ±5 mm、預製 ±3 mm、安裝 ±10 mm，√(5² + 3² + 10²) = √134 ≈ ±11.6 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Combine position errors for one object by root-sum-square: set-out ±5 mm, fabrication ±3 mm and installation ±10 mm give √(5² + 3² + 10²) = √134 ≈ ±11.6 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「模型協調完成後，現場只要照圖施工就不會有空間衝突。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once the model is coordinated, building to the drawings cannot produce space conflicts.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「現場放樣與公差累積」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Site set-out and tolerance stack”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-29-k1","title":"現場安裝公差與模型驗證","titleEn":"Installation tolerances and field verification of the model","text":"模型中相距幾公釐的兩個物件，在現場可能因放樣、預製尺寸與安裝誤差而相撞。因此協調後的模型要經由全測站或雷射掃描回到現場：先以模型座標放樣吊架與套管位置，安裝後再量測實際位置與模型比對。","textEn":"Two objects a few millimetres apart in the model can collide on site because of set-out, fabrication and installation errors. The coordinated model must therefore return to site through total stations or laser scanning: hangers and sleeves are set out from model coordinates, and after installation actual positions are measured and compared with the model.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模型協調完成後，現場只要照圖施工就不會有空間衝突。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once the model is coordinated, building to the drawings cannot produce space conflicts. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「現場安裝公差與模型驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Installation tolerances and field verification of the model\" is correct?","options":["模型協調完成後，現場只要照圖施工就不會有空間衝突。","共用資料環境只是存放檔案的雲端資料夾。","模型中相距幾公釐的兩個物件，在現場可能因放樣、預製尺寸與安裝誤差而相撞。"],"optionsEn":["Once the model is coordinated, building to the drawings cannot produce space conflicts.","A common data environment is just a cloud folder for storing files.","Two objects a few millimetres apart in the model can collide on site because of set-out, fabrication and installation errors."],"answer":2,"explanation":"模型中相距幾公釐的兩個物件，在現場可能因放樣、預製尺寸與安裝誤差而相撞。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Two objects a few millimetres apart in the model can collide on site because of set-out, fabrication and installation errors. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b096-v13-30","title":"現場安裝公差與模型驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Installation tolerances and field verification of the model: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「現場放樣與公差累積」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Site set-out and tolerance stack” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：單一物件位置誤差以平方和開根號合成：放樣 ±5 mm、預製 ±3 mm、安裝 ±10 mm，√(5² + 3² + 10²) = √134 ≈ ±11.6 mm。兩個獨立安裝物件之間的相對誤差約 √2×11.6 ≈ ±16.4 mm，所以模型淨距小於約 16 mm 處現場就有明顯碰撞機率，軟碰撞規則宜取 20 至 25 mm。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Combine position errors for one object by root-sum-square: set-out ±5 mm, fabrication ±3 mm and installation ±10 mm give √(5² + 3² + 10²) = √134 ≈ ±11.6 mm. Between two independently installed objects the relative error is about √2×11.6 ≈ ±16.4 mm, so where the model gap is below about 16 mm a site clash is quite likely, and a clearance rule of 20 to 25 mm is sensible. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以機器人全測站從模型匯出點位放樣吊架、套管與預埋件，放樣後抽查實際位置；安裝完成後以雷射掃描或全測站量測關鍵管線，與模型比對並列出超過容許值的位置，作為封板前的檢查點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Set out hangers, sleeves and embeds from model points with a robotic total station and spot-check the marks; after installation measure key services by laser scanning or total station, compare with the model and list locations beyond tolerance as a check before the ceiling closes up.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"單一物件位置誤差以平方和開根號合成：放樣 ±5 mm、預製 ±3 mm、安裝 ±10 mm，√(5² + 3² + 10²) = √134 ≈ ±11.6 mm。兩個獨立安裝物件之間的相對誤差約 √2×11.6 ≈ ±16.4 mm，所以模型淨距小於約 16 mm 處現場就有明顯碰撞機率，軟碰撞規則宜取 20 至 25 mm。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Combine position errors for one object by root-sum-square: set-out ±5 mm, fabrication ±3 mm and installation ±10 mm give √(5² + 3² + 10²) = √134 ≈ ±11.6 mm. Between two independently installed objects the relative error is about √2×11.6 ≈ ±16.4 mm, so where the model gap is below about 16 mm a site clash is quite likely, and a clearance rule of 20 to 25 mm is sensible. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「現場安裝公差與模型驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Installation tolerances and field verification of the model\", which statement holds?","options":["單一物件位置誤差以平方和開根號合成：放樣 ±5 mm、預製 ±3 mm、安裝 ±10 mm，√(5² + 3² + 10²) = √134 ≈ ±11.6 mm。","碰撞檢查的主要目的是找建模錯誤，與樓高設計無關。","碰撞報告為零，就代表現場一定可以順利安裝。"],"optionsEn":["Combine position errors for one object by root-sum-square: set-out ±5 mm, fabrication ±3 mm and installation ±10 mm give √(5² + 3² + 10²) = √134 ≈ ±11.6 mm.","Clash detection is mainly for catching modelling mistakes and has nothing to do with storey-height design.","A clash report of zero guarantees smooth installation on site."],"answer":0,"explanation":"單一物件位置誤差以平方和開根號合成：放樣 ±5 mm、預製 ±3 mm、安裝 ±10 mm，√(5² + 3² + 10²) = √134 ≈ ±11.6 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Combine position errors for one object by root-sum-square: set-out ±5 mm, fabrication ±3 mm and installation ±10 mm give √(5² + 3² + 10²) = √134 ≈ ±11.6 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b096-v13-31","title":"現場安裝公差與模型驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Installation tolerances and field verification of the model: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「現場放樣與公差累積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Site set-out and tolerance stack” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以機器人全測站從模型匯出點位放樣吊架、套管與預埋件，放樣後抽查實際位置；安裝完成後以雷射掃描或全測站量測關鍵管線，與模型比對並列出超過容許值的位置，作為封板前的檢查點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Set out hangers, sleeves and embeds from model points with a robotic total station and spot-check the marks; after installation measure key services by laser scanning or total station, compare with the model and list locations beyond tolerance as a check before the ceiling closes up. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：規定封板前量測為保留點：天花板、管道間與牆面封板前，必須完成關鍵管線位置量測並與模型比對，偏差超過容許值者由設計與施工雙方確認處置後才能封閉。","observationEn":"Site practice: Make pre-close-up survey a hold point: before ceilings, shafts or walls are closed, key services must be measured and compared with the model, and any deviation beyond tolerance must be resolved jointly by design and construction before closing.","failure":"注意干擾：模型協調完美，現場卻仍用捲尺從柱面量測放樣，累積誤差讓多支管線偏移數公分，與後續施工的電纜架相撞；因為沒有安裝後量測，問題到天花板封板時才被發現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: The model is perfectly coordinated but site crews still set out with tapes from column faces, accumulated errors shift several pipes by centimetres into later cable trays, and with no post-installation survey the problem surfaces only when the ceiling is boarded. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以機器人全測站從模型匯出點位放樣吊架、套管與預埋件，放樣後抽查實際位置；安裝完成後以雷射掃描或全測站量測關鍵管線，與模型比對並列出超過容許值的位置，作為封板前的檢查點。","textEn":"Set out hangers, sleeves and embeds from model points with a robotic total station and spot-check the marks; after installation measure key services by laser scanning or total station, compare with the model and list locations beyond tolerance as a check before the ceiling closes up.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"規定封板前量測為保留點：天花板、管道間與牆面封板前，必須完成關鍵管線位置量測並與模型比對，偏差超過容許值者由設計與施工雙方確認處置後才能封閉。","textEn":"Make pre-close-up survey a hold point: before ceilings, shafts or walls are closed, key services must be measured and compared with the model, and any deviation beyond tolerance must be resolved jointly by design and construction before closing.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「現場安裝公差與模型驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Installation tolerances and field verification of the model\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以機器人全測站從模型匯出點位放樣吊架、套管與預埋件，放樣後抽查實際位置。","碰撞報告產出後，軟體會自動決定哪個專業必須修改。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Set out hangers, sleeves and embeds from model points with a robotic total station and spot-check the marks.","Once the clash report is produced, the software decides which discipline must change."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以機器人全測站從模型匯出點位放樣吊架、套管與預埋件，放樣後抽查實際位置；安裝完成後以雷射掃描或全測站量測關鍵管線，與模型比對並列出超過容許值的位置，作為封板前的檢查點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Set out hangers, sleeves and embeds from model points with a robotic total station and spot-check the marks; after installation measure key services by laser scanning or total station, compare with the model and list locations beyond tolerance as a check before the ceiling closes up. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b096-v13-32","title":"現場安裝公差與模型驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Installation tolerances and field verification of the model: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「現場放樣與公差累積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Site set-out and tolerance stack” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"模型協調完美，現場卻仍用捲尺從柱面量測放樣，累積誤差讓多支管線偏移數公分，與後續施工的電纜架相撞；因為沒有安裝後量測，問題到天花板封板時才被發現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"The model is perfectly coordinated but site crews still set out with tapes from column faces, accumulated errors shift several pipes by centimetres into later cable trays, and with no post-installation survey the problem surfaces only when the ceiling is boarded. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這一步把虛擬協調與實體施工連成閉環，也讓軟碰撞淨距有了依據：淨距應涵蓋各項誤差的合成，而不是任意的數字。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This closes the loop between virtual coordination and physical construction and gives the clearance rules a basis, since the clearance should cover the combined errors rather than an arbitrary number.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模型協調完成後，現場只要照圖施工就不會有空間衝突。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once the model is coordinated, building to the drawings cannot produce space conflicts.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"模型協調完美，現場卻仍用捲尺從柱面量測放樣，累積誤差讓多支管線偏移數公分，與後續施工的電纜架相撞；因為沒有安裝後量測，問題到天花板封板時才被發現。","textEn":"The model is perfectly coordinated but site crews still set out with tapes from column faces, accumulated errors shift several pipes by centimetres into later cable trays, and with no post-installation survey the problem surfaces only when the ceiling is boarded.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「現場安裝公差與模型驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Installation tolerances and field verification of the model\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","共用資料環境只是存放檔案的雲端資料夾。","模型協調完美，現場卻仍用捲尺從柱面量測放樣，累積誤差讓多支管線偏移數公分，與後續施工的電纜架相撞；因為沒有安裝後量測，問題到天花板封板時才被發現。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A common data environment is just a cloud folder for storing files.","The model is perfectly coordinated but site crews still set out with tapes from column faces, accumulated errors shift several pipes by centimetres into later cable trays, and with no post-installation survey the problem surfaces only when the ceiling is boarded."],"answer":2,"explanation":"模型協調完美，現場卻仍用捲尺從柱面量測放樣，累積誤差讓多支管線偏移數公分，與後續施工的電纜架相撞；因為沒有安裝後量測，問題到天花板封板時才被發現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"The model is perfectly coordinated but site crews still set out with tapes from column faces, accumulated errors shift several pipes by centimetres into later cable trays, and with no post-installation survey the problem surfaces only when the ceiling is boarded. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b096-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「設計變更下的模型維護」與「竣工模型與資產資訊交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Model maintenance under design change\" and \"As-built models and asset-information handover\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b096-v13-33","title":"設計變更下的模型維護：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Model maintenance under design change: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「共用資料環境狀態」如何影響工程數位模型碰撞檢查的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “CDE states and change control” governs force, deformation or durability in “BIM-based construction clash detection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"設計變更、送審意見與現場問題會讓模型持續修改，若沒有版本控制，碰撞檢查可能拿新版結構對舊版機電比較而得出錯誤結論。ISO 19650 把資訊容器分成作業中、共享、發布與封存等狀態：只有經過檢核並轉為共享的模型才能進入聯合，只有發布版本才能作為施工依據；每次狀態轉換都要記錄版本與核准人，讓任何一份碰撞報告都能追溯到確切的模型版本。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「共用資料環境狀態」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Design changes, review comments and site issues keep the models changing, and without version control a clash run may compare a new structure against an old MEP model and reach wrong conclusions. ISO 19650 divides information containers into work-in-progress, shared, published and archived states: only checked models moved to shared may enter federation, and only published revisions may be built from, with every state change recording the revision and approver so that any clash report can be traced to exact model versions. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “CDE states and change control” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：聯合模型含 12 個專業模型，若每個模型準時以當週版本上傳的機率為 90%，全部都是當週版本的機率只有 0.9^12 ≈ 0.28；訂定固定凍結時間、把準時率提高到 98% 後，機率升為 0.98^12 ≈ 0.78。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A federated model contains 12 discipline models; if each is uploaded on time with that week's revision with probability 90%, the chance that all are current is only 0.9^12 ≈ 0.28; a fixed freeze time that lifts on-time delivery to 98% raises it to 0.98^12 ≈ 0.78.","failure":"常見誤解：「共用資料環境只是存放檔案的雲端資料夾。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A common data environment is just a cloud folder for storing files.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「共用資料環境狀態」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “CDE states and change control”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-33-k1","title":"設計變更下的模型維護","titleEn":"Model maintenance under design change","text":"設計變更、送審意見與現場問題會讓模型持續修改，若沒有版本控制，碰撞檢查可能拿新版結構對舊版機電比較而得出錯誤結論。ISO 19650 把資訊容器分成作業中、共享、發布與封存等狀態：只有經過檢核並轉為共享的模型才能進入聯合，只有發布版本才能作為施工依據；每次狀態轉換都要記錄版本與核准人，讓任何一份碰撞報告都能追溯到確切的模型版本。","textEn":"Design changes, review comments and site issues keep the models changing, and without version control a clash run may compare a new structure against an old MEP model and reach wrong conclusions. ISO 19650 divides information containers into work-in-progress, shared, published and archived states: only checked models moved to shared may enter federation, and only published revisions may be built from, with every state change recording the revision and approver so that any clash report can be traced to exact model versions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：共用資料環境只是存放檔案的雲端資料夾。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A common data environment is just a cloud folder for storing files. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「設計變更下的模型維護」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Model maintenance under design change\" is correct?","options":["設計變更、送審意見與現場問題會讓模型持續修改，若沒有版本控制，碰撞檢查可能拿新版結構對舊版機電比較而得出錯誤結論。","共用資料環境只是存放檔案的雲端資料夾。","施工期間協調用的模型就等於竣工模型。"],"optionsEn":["Design changes, review comments and site issues keep the models changing, and without version control a clash run may compare a new structure against an old MEP model and reach wrong conclusions.","A common data environment is just a cloud folder for storing files.","The model used for coordination during construction is the as-built model."],"answer":0,"explanation":"設計變更、送審意見與現場問題會讓模型持續修改，若沒有版本控制，碰撞檢查可能拿新版結構對舊版機電比較而得出錯誤結論。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Design changes, review comments and site issues keep the models changing, and without version control a clash run may compare a new structure against an old MEP model and reach wrong conclusions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b096-v13-34","title":"設計變更下的模型維護：定量估算","titleEn":"Model maintenance under design change: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「共用資料環境狀態」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “CDE states and change control” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：聯合模型含 12 個專業模型，若每個模型準時以當週版本上傳的機率為 90%，全部都是當週版本的機率只有 0.9^12 ≈ 0.28；訂定固定凍結時間、把準時率提高到 98% 後，機率升為 0.98^12 ≈ 0.78。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A federated model contains 12 discipline models; if each is uploaded on time with that week's revision with probability 90%, the chance that all are current is only 0.9^12 ≈ 0.28; a fixed freeze time that lifts on-time delivery to 98% raises it to 0.98^12 ≈ 0.78. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每份碰撞報告封面列出所有參與模型的檔名、版本號與狀態，資訊管理者在聯合前與共用資料環境的發布紀錄比對；設計變更單要列出受影響區域，並觸發該區域重新協調與重新簽認。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Every clash report cover lists the file name, revision and status of every model used, and the information manager checks them against the common data environment's publication record before federation; each design change notice must list affected areas and trigger re-coordination and re-sign-off of those areas.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"聯合模型含 12 個專業模型，若每個模型準時以當週版本上傳的機率為 90%，全部都是當週版本的機率只有 0.9^12 ≈ 0.28；訂定固定凍結時間、把準時率提高到 98% 後，機率升為 0.98^12 ≈ 0.78。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A federated model contains 12 discipline models; if each is uploaded on time with that week's revision with probability 90%, the chance that all are current is only 0.9^12 ≈ 0.28; a fixed freeze time that lifts on-time delivery to 98% raises it to 0.98^12 ≈ 0.78. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「設計變更下的模型維護」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Model maintenance under design change\", which statement holds?","options":["只要把所有檔案匯入同一個軟體，模型就會自動對齊。","聯合模型含 12 個專業模型，若每個模型準時以當週版本上傳的機率為 90%，全部都是當週版本的機率只有 0.9^12 ≈ 0.28。","所有元素都要做到最高的模型發展程度，碰撞檢查才有意義。"],"optionsEn":["Importing every file into the same software aligns the models automatically.","A federated model contains 12 discipline models.","Every element must reach the highest level of development for clash detection to be meaningful."],"answer":1,"explanation":"聯合模型含 12 個專業模型，若每個模型準時以當週版本上傳的機率為 90%，全部都是當週版本的機率只有 0.9^12 ≈ 0.28；訂定固定凍結時間、把準時率提高到 98% 後，機率升為 0.98^12 ≈ 0.78。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A federated model contains 12 discipline models; if each is uploaded on time with that week's revision with probability 90%, the chance that all are current is only 0.9^12 ≈ 0.28; a fixed freeze time that lifts on-time delivery to 98% raises it to 0.98^12 ≈ 0.78. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b096-v13-35","title":"設計變更下的模型維護：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Model maintenance under design change: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「共用資料環境狀態」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “CDE states and change control” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每份碰撞報告封面列出所有參與模型的檔名、版本號與狀態，資訊管理者在聯合前與共用資料環境的發布紀錄比對；設計變更單要列出受影響區域，並觸發該區域重新協調與重新簽認。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Every clash report cover lists the file name, revision and status of every model used, and the information manager checks them against the common data environment's publication record before federation; each design change notice must list affected areas and trigger re-coordination and re-sign-off of those areas. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在合約中明定模型與圖說的優先順序與同步規則，訂定每週固定的模型凍結時間；設計變更通知必須同時附上更新後的模型版本，否則不得發布。","observationEn":"Site practice: State in the contract the precedence and synchronisation rules between models and drawings and set a fixed weekly model-freeze time; a design change notice may not be issued without the updated model revision attached.","failure":"注意干擾：變更只更新了圖說而未更新模型，或反之，使模型與圖說不一致；施工依圖說做、協調依模型做，雙方都以為自己正確，衝突到現場才出現，責任歸屬也難以釐清。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A change that updates the drawings but not the model, or the reverse, leaves the two inconsistent; construction follows the drawings while coordination follows the model, each side believes it is right, the conflict surfaces on site and responsibility is hard to establish. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每份碰撞報告封面列出所有參與模型的檔名、版本號與狀態，資訊管理者在聯合前與共用資料環境的發布紀錄比對；設計變更單要列出受影響區域，並觸發該區域重新協調與重新簽認。","textEn":"Every clash report cover lists the file name, revision and status of every model used, and the information manager checks them against the common data environment's publication record before federation; each design change notice must list affected areas and trigger re-coordination and re-sign-off of those areas.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在合約中明定模型與圖說的優先順序與同步規則，訂定每週固定的模型凍結時間；設計變更通知必須同時附上更新後的模型版本，否則不得發布。","textEn":"State in the contract the precedence and synchronisation rules between models and drawings and set a fixed weekly model-freeze time; a design change notice may not be issued without the updated model revision attached.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「設計變更下的模型維護」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Model maintenance under design change\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只要三維模型沒有碰撞，施工順序就不會發生衝突。","每份碰撞報告封面列出所有參與模型的檔名、版本號與狀態，資訊管理者在聯合前與共用資料環境的發布紀錄比對。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","If the 3D model has no clashes, the construction sequence cannot conflict.","Every clash report cover lists the file name, revision and status of every model used, and the information manager checks them against the common data environment's publication record before federation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每份碰撞報告封面列出所有參與模型的檔名、版本號與狀態，資訊管理者在聯合前與共用資料環境的發布紀錄比對；設計變更單要列出受影響區域，並觸發該區域重新協調與重新簽認。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Every clash report cover lists the file name, revision and status of every model used, and the information manager checks them against the common data environment's publication record before federation; each design change notice must list affected areas and trigger re-coordination and re-sign-off of those areas. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b096-v13-36","title":"設計變更下的模型維護：失效診斷","titleEn":"Model maintenance under design change: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「共用資料環境狀態」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “CDE states and change control” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"變更只更新了圖說而未更新模型，或反之，使模型與圖說不一致；施工依圖說做、協調依模型做，雙方都以為自己正確，衝突到現場才出現，責任歸屬也難以釐清。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A change that updates the drawings but not the model, or the reverse, leaves the two inconsistent; construction follows the drawings while coordination follows the model, each side believes it is right, the conflict surfaces on site and responsibility is hard to establish. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：ISO 19650 把資訊容器分成作業中、共享、發布與封存等狀態：只有經過檢核並轉為共享的模型才能進入聯合，只有發布版本才能作為施工依據；每次狀態轉換都要記錄版本與核准人，讓任何一份碰撞報告都能追溯到確切的模型版本。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: ISO 19650 divides information containers into work-in-progress, shared, published and archived states: only checked models moved to shared may enter federation, and only published revisions may be built from, with every state change recording the revision and approver so that any clash report can be traced to exact model versions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「共用資料環境只是存放檔案的雲端資料夾。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A common data environment is just a cloud folder for storing files.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"變更只更新了圖說而未更新模型，或反之，使模型與圖說不一致；施工依圖說做、協調依模型做，雙方都以為自己正確，衝突到現場才出現，責任歸屬也難以釐清。","textEn":"A change that updates the drawings but not the model, or the reverse, leaves the two inconsistent; construction follows the drawings while coordination follows the model, each side believes it is right, the conflict surfaces on site and responsibility is hard to establish.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「設計變更下的模型維護」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Model maintenance under design change\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["變更只更新了圖說而未更新模型，或反之，使模型與圖說不一致；施工依圖說做、協調依模型做，雙方都以為自己正確，衝突到現場才出現，責任歸屬也難以釐清。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","施工期間協調用的模型就等於竣工模型。"],"optionsEn":["A change that updates the drawings but not the model, or the reverse, leaves the two inconsistent.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The model used for coordination during construction is the as-built model."],"answer":0,"explanation":"變更只更新了圖說而未更新模型，或反之，使模型與圖說不一致；施工依圖說做、協調依模型做，雙方都以為自己正確，衝突到現場才出現，責任歸屬也難以釐清。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A change that updates the drawings but not the model, or the reverse, leaves the two inconsistent; construction follows the drawings while coordination follows the model, each side believes it is right, the conflict surfaces on site and responsibility is hard to establish. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b096-v13-37","title":"竣工模型與資產資訊交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"As-built models and asset-information handover: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資訊模型」如何影響工程數位模型碰撞檢查的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset information model” governs force, deformation or durability in “BIM-based construction clash detection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"協調後的模型若在交接時只留下幾何，營運者仍找不到閥門、維修淨空與設備資料。交接應把模型轉成資產資訊模型：依資產分類賦予編碼、廠牌、型號、保固與維護週期，並保留碰撞協調中確認的維修通道與淨空。Crossrail 中央段九座主要車站每站約有 15,000 至 25,000 個資產，說明交接資料量之大，必須以資料規則自動檢查，不能只靠人工逐一核對。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「資產資訊模型」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"If the coordinated model leaves handover with geometry only, operators still cannot find valves, maintenance clearances or equipment data. Handover should turn the model into an asset information model: assign classification codes, makes, models, warranties and maintenance intervals by asset, and keep the access routes and clearances confirmed during clash coordination. The nine main Crossrail central-section stations each had about 15,000 to 25,000 assets, showing how large handover data becomes and why it must be checked by automated data rules rather than by hand alone. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Asset information model” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：9 站 × 每站 15,000 至 25,000 個資產 = 135,000 至 225,000 個資產；每個資產 20 項屬性時共 2.7 至 4.5 百萬筆資料。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: 9 stations × 15,000 to 25,000 assets each = 135,000 to 225,000 assets; with 20 attributes per asset that is 2.7 to 4.5 million values.","failure":"常見誤解：「施工期間協調用的模型就等於竣工模型。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The model used for coordination during construction is the as-built model.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「資產資訊模型」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Asset information model”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-37-k1","title":"竣工模型與資產資訊交接","titleEn":"As-built models and asset-information handover","text":"協調後的模型若在交接時只留下幾何，營運者仍找不到閥門、維修淨空與設備資料。交接應把模型轉成資產資訊模型：依資產分類賦予編碼、廠牌、型號、保固與維護週期，並保留碰撞協調中確認的維修通道與淨空。","textEn":"If the coordinated model leaves handover with geometry only, operators still cannot find valves, maintenance clearances or equipment data. Handover should turn the model into an asset information model: assign classification codes, makes, models, warranties and maintenance intervals by asset, and keep the access routes and clearances confirmed during clash coordination.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：施工期間協調用的模型就等於竣工模型。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The model used for coordination during construction is the as-built model. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「竣工模型與資產資訊交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"As-built models and asset-information handover\" is correct?","options":["施工期間協調用的模型就等於竣工模型。","協調後的模型若在交接時只留下幾何，營運者仍找不到閥門、維修淨空與設備資料。","碰撞檢查的主要目的是找建模錯誤，與樓高設計無關。"],"optionsEn":["The model used for coordination during construction is the as-built model.","If the coordinated model leaves handover with geometry only, operators still cannot find valves, maintenance clearances or equipment data.","Clash detection is mainly for catching modelling mistakes and has nothing to do with storey-height design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"協調後的模型若在交接時只留下幾何，營運者仍找不到閥門、維修淨空與設備資料。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"If the coordinated model leaves handover with geometry only, operators still cannot find valves, maintenance clearances or equipment data. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b096-v13-38","title":"竣工模型與資產資訊交接：定量估算","titleEn":"As-built models and asset-information handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資訊模型」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset information model” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：9 站 × 每站 15,000 至 25,000 個資產 = 135,000 至 225,000 個資產；每個資產 20 項屬性時共 2.7 至 4.5 百萬筆資料。即使正確率 99.5%，仍有 0.005×2,700,000 = 13,500 至 0.005×4,500,000 = 22,500 筆錯誤。屬性數與正確率為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: 9 stations × 15,000 to 25,000 assets each = 135,000 to 225,000 assets; with 20 attributes per asset that is 2.7 to 4.5 million values. Even at 99.5% accuracy there remain 0.005×2,700,000 = 13,500 to 0.005×4,500,000 = 22,500 wrong values. Attribute count and accuracy are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：依交接資訊需求建立自動檢查規則（必填屬性、編碼格式、空間歸屬、與設備清單的一致性），每批交付都產出通過率報告；並抽樣到現場核對模型中的資產編號、位置與銘牌，確認竣工模型反映實際安裝，而非協調時的設計意圖。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build automated checks from the handover information requirements (mandatory attributes, code formats, space assignment, consistency with equipment schedules), produce a pass-rate report for every delivery, and sample assets on site to compare model tags, positions and nameplates, confirming that the as-built model reflects what was installed rather than the design intent at coordination.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"9 站 × 每站 15,000 至 25,000 個資產 = 135,000 至 225,000 個資產；每個資產 20 項屬性時共 2.7 至 4.5 百萬筆資料。即使正確率 99.5%，仍有 0.005×2,700,000 = 13,500 至 0.005×4,500,000 = 22,500 筆錯誤。屬性數與正確率為教學假設。","textEn":"9 stations × 15,000 to 25,000 assets each = 135,000 to 225,000 assets; with 20 attributes per asset that is 2.7 to 4.5 million values. Even at 99.5% accuracy there remain 0.005×2,700,000 = 13,500 to 0.005×4,500,000 = 22,500 wrong values. Attribute count and accuracy are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「竣工模型與資產資訊交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"As-built models and asset-information handover\", which statement holds?","options":["碰撞報告為零，就代表現場一定可以順利安裝。","碰撞報告產出後，軟體會自動決定哪個專業必須修改。","9 站 × 每站 15,000 至 25,000 個資產 = 135,000 至 225,000 個資產。"],"optionsEn":["A clash report of zero guarantees smooth installation on site.","Once the clash report is produced, the software decides which discipline must change.","9 stations × 15,000 to 25,000 assets each = 135,000 to 225,000 assets; with 20 attributes per asset that is 2.7 to 4.5 million values."],"answer":2,"explanation":"9 站 × 每站 15,000 至 25,000 個資產 = 135,000 至 225,000 個資產；每個資產 20 項屬性時共 2.7 至 4.5 百萬筆資料。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"9 stations × 15,000 to 25,000 assets each = 135,000 to 225,000 assets; with 20 attributes per asset that is 2.7 to 4.5 million values. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b096-v13-39","title":"竣工模型與資產資訊交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"As-built models and asset-information handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資訊模型」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset information model” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"依交接資訊需求建立自動檢查規則（必填屬性、編碼格式、空間歸屬、與設備清單的一致性），每批交付都產出通過率報告；並抽樣到現場核對模型中的資產編號、位置與銘牌，確認竣工模型反映實際安裝，而非協調時的設計意圖。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build automated checks from the handover information requirements (mandatory attributes, code formats, space assignment, consistency with equipment schedules), produce a pass-rate report for every delivery, and sample assets on site to compare model tags, positions and nameplates, confirming that the as-built model reflects what was installed rather than the design intent at coordination. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接資訊需求要在招標時寫入合約，指定格式（例如 IFC 與 COBie）、屬性清單與驗收門檻；竣工模型須經現場抽驗與業主營運代表簽認，才能作為最後付款條件之一。","observationEn":"Site practice: Write handover information requirements into the contract at tender, specifying formats (for example IFC and COBie), attribute lists and acceptance thresholds; the as-built model must pass site sampling and sign-off by the owner's operations representative before it counts toward final payment.","failure":"注意干擾：所謂竣工模型其實是最後一版協調模型，未反映現場改線，營運單位依模型打開天花板找閥門卻撲空；資產屬性缺漏使維護系統無法匯入，業主只好另外花錢重新盤點。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An ‘as-built’ model that is really the last coordination model, missing site re-routes, sends operators opening ceilings to find valves that are not there; missing asset attributes stop the maintenance system from importing data, and the owner pays again for a fresh survey. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"依交接資訊需求建立自動檢查規則（必填屬性、編碼格式、空間歸屬、與設備清單的一致性），每批交付都產出通過率報告；並抽樣到現場核對模型中的資產編號、位置與銘牌，確認竣工模型反映實際安裝，而非協調時的設計意圖。","textEn":"Build automated checks from the handover information requirements (mandatory attributes, code formats, space assignment, consistency with equipment schedules), produce a pass-rate report for every delivery, and sample assets on site to compare model tags, positions and nameplates, confirming that the as-built model reflects what was installed rather than the design intent at coordination.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接資訊需求要在招標時寫入合約，指定格式（例如 IFC 與 COBie）、屬性清單與驗收門檻；竣工模型須經現場抽驗與業主營運代表簽認，才能作為最後付款條件之一。","textEn":"Write handover information requirements into the contract at tender, specifying formats (for example IFC and COBie), attribute lists and acceptance thresholds; the as-built model must pass site sampling and sign-off by the owner's operations representative before it counts toward final payment.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「竣工模型與資產資訊交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"As-built models and asset-information handover\"?","options":["依交接資訊需求建立自動檢查規則（必填屬性、編碼格式、空間歸屬、與設備清單的一致性），每批交付都產出通過率報告。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","碰撞數量越少，代表協調品質越好。"],"optionsEn":["Build automated checks from the handover information requirements (mandatory attributes, code formats, space assignment, consistency with equipment schedules), produce a pass-rate report for every delivery, and sample assets on site to compare model tags, positions and nameplates, confirming that the as-built model reflects what was installed rather than the design intent at coordination.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The fewer the clashes in the report, the better the coordination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"依交接資訊需求建立自動檢查規則（必填屬性、編碼格式、空間歸屬、與設備清單的一致性），每批交付都產出通過率報告；並抽樣到現場核對模型中的資產編號、位置與銘牌，確認竣工模型反映實際安裝，而非協調時的設計意圖。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build automated checks from the handover information requirements (mandatory attributes, code formats, space assignment, consistency with equipment schedules), produce a pass-rate report for every delivery, and sample assets on site to compare model tags, positions and nameplates, confirming that the as-built model reflects what was installed rather than the design intent at coordination. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b096-v13-40","title":"竣工模型與資產資訊交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"As-built models and asset-information handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b096-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資訊模型」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset information model” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"所謂竣工模型其實是最後一版協調模型，未反映現場改線，營運單位依模型打開天花板找閥門卻撲空；資產屬性缺漏使維護系統無法匯入，業主只好另外花錢重新盤點。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An ‘as-built’ model that is really the last coordination model, missing site re-routes, sends operators opening ceilings to find valves that are not there; missing asset attributes stop the maintenance system from importing data, and the owner pays again for a fresh survey. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：Crossrail 中央段九座主要車站每站約有 15,000 至 25,000 個資產，說明交接資料量之大，必須以資料規則自動檢查，不能只靠人工逐一核對。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The nine main Crossrail central-section stations each had about 15,000 to 25,000 assets, showing how large handover data becomes and why it must be checked by automated data rules rather than by hand alone.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「施工期間協調用的模型就等於竣工模型。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The model used for coordination during construction is the as-built model.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b096-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"所謂竣工模型其實是最後一版協調模型，未反映現場改線，營運單位依模型打開天花板找閥門卻撲空；資產屬性缺漏使維護系統無法匯入，業主只好另外花錢重新盤點。","textEn":"An ‘as-built’ model that is really the last coordination model, missing site re-routes, sends operators opening ceilings to find valves that are not there; missing asset attributes stop the maintenance system from importing data, and the owner pays again for a fresh survey.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]},{"id":"b096-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「竣工模型與資產資訊交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"As-built models and asset-information handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","所謂竣工模型其實是最後一版協調模型，未反映現場改線，營運單位依模型打開天花板找閥門卻撲空；資產屬性缺漏使維護系統無法匯入，業主只好另外花錢重新盤點。","碰撞檢查的主要目的是找建模錯誤，與樓高設計無關。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","An ‘as-built’ model that is really the last coordination model, missing site re-routes, sends operators opening ceilings to find valves that are not there.","Clash detection is mainly for catching modelling mistakes and has nothing to do with storey-height design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"所謂竣工模型其實是最後一版協調模型，未反映現場改線，營運單位依模型打開天花板找閥門卻撲空；資產屬性缺漏使維護系統無法匯入，業主只好另外花錢重新盤點。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An ‘as-built’ model that is really the last coordination model, missing site re-routes, sends operators opening ceilings to find valves that are not there; missing asset attributes stop the maintenance system from importing data, and the owner pays again for a fresh survey. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-crossrail-bim-lessons","v13s-crossrail-cad","v13s-flv-building","v13s-buildingsmart-bcf","v13s-itcon-mep-vdc"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
